mission "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 1"
	landing
	name "Track down stolen wedding gifts"
	description "Look for a stolen shipment of wedding gifts meant for House Myurej on <destination>."
	source Raaqa-Kvelq-Ryuit
	destination Kasii-Tuur-Saqru
	to offer
		or
			and
				has "Successors: Ghosts Prelude Wedding: offered"
				random < 40
			and
				has "Successors: Ghosts Prelude Wedding: offered"
				has "Successors: Ghosts 4: offered"
	on offer
		conversation
			`While walking in the spaceport here, you are pulled aside by a pair of House Myurej military officers. "Come with us," one says, "thou shalt not be harmed, but thou hast a private meeting waiting thou needest attend."`
			choice
				`	(Go with them.)`
				`	(Run away.)`
					goto run
			`	The two take you to a dense nest of shops and hotels on a hill overlooking one of the massive spaceport's loading docks; it lies what must be more than a hundred meters below. A web of canals interleaves the regularly-misted streets, and looking inside, you can see groups of Successors swimming in various directions, occasionally emerging onto the terrestrial paths and shaking off water from the hydrophobic fabrics of their clothing. You are led to a small, comfortable-looking hotel overlooking one of these canals, and deposited in a medium-sized oblong room, divided roughly in half by an oily-colored fabric screen. The guards motion for you to sit on a chair on one side of it, and you comply.`
			`	From the other side of the screen comes a slow voice that your translation device duly rearranges into your language: "Captain <first> <last>, I believe?"`
			choice
				`	"Yes?"`
				`	"Who's asking?"`
			`	"House Myurej longs to exercise thy services. Something belonging to us was stolen. Thou shalt be compensated for its safe return. Doth this interest thee?" The screen shimmers in one long, glittery wave. Behind you, one of the guards shuffles.`
			`	"You're going to have to give me more than that," you say.`
			`	The wave rebounds off the far wall and retraces its way back down the screen. "Hast thou before entered into the bonds of matrimony?" the voice says. Before you can respond, it continues. "'Tis customary, when one doth, for the celebrants to render some minor gifts upon the duly unified, a commemoration of the families' intertwining evermore. To steal such trinkets would be a base and wretched act - a child-race as yours should still conceive of that." The wave continues to echo, back and forth. "A certain knave'f the so-called People's Houses thought it wise to thus insult this happy House, on the eve of another day of joy, no doubt thinking with a dead mind they lay beyond our reach. Bring back our gifts, and we shall pay thee..." The voice pauses for a while, as if away in thought. "And perhaps thou wilt have earned a favor, though alien thou mightst be."`
			choice
				`	"Why ask me?"`
				`	"How much are you going to pay me?"`
					goto pay
				`	"All right, I'll do it."`
					goto yes
				`	"Sorry, but I don't want any part of this."`
					goto no
			branch kaatrij
				has "successors kaatrij patron"
			`	"Riijaaora of House Sioeora speaks well of thee, dost thou know? Thy reliability, thy strength of will. They say thou'rt capable of this task, and we know thou'rt uniquely suited to it. Wilt thou accept?"`
				goto "follow up"
			label kaatrij
			`	"After thou fail'dst Sioeora as thou did'st, thinks thee? Nonetheless, thou'rt more suitable to our needs than any other. Shouldst thou decline, we shall simply move on to the next. So, wilt thou accept?"`
				goto "follow up"
			label pay
			`	The voice hums briefly. "Four hundred thousand credits," they say, "not to be negotiated. Dost thou accept?"`
			label "follow up"
			choice
				`	"All right, I'll do it."`
				`	"Sorry, but I don't want any part of this."`
					goto no
			label yes
			action
				log "People" "Riiria" "One of the most influential members of the People's Houses of the Successors. They personally control a substantial portion of Kasii-Tuur-Saqru via a mix of charismatic leadership and brute strength. Suspected of hijacking a transport of gifts for the upcoming wedding between scions of Houses Myurej and Chydiyi."
				log "Accepted an offer by House Myurej to track down and recover a shipment of wedding gifts stolen by a member of the People's Houses."
			`	The shimmering wave seems like it's losing energy now, growing slower and fainter with each cycle back and forth. "Excellent," says the voice. "The quarry thou shouldst seek on Kasii-Tuur-Saqru is by name Riiria, a well-known thief and useful fool. Shouldst thy own powers of searching fail thee, we've a friend of the House there too, a sharp-eyed merchant captain eager to get involved in things they think to be rewarding. Our agents here shall see that thou receiv'st the details at thy ship." You hear the rustling of fabric and the faint wet slithering of a Successor moving. The guards behind you relax and, as you turn to look at them, they gesture towards the door. Before you leave, the voice speaks one last time. "Do not fail us, captain."`
			`	You are escorted back to the edge of the residential area by the guards, who leave you to find your own way back to your ship. As the ground crew finish up their refueling and maintenance of the <ship>, one of them hands you a data-sphere containing information about Riiria and House Myurej's contact on Kasii-Tuur-Saqru.`
				accept

			label run
			`	Kicking a stone to the side to distract the pair, you dash into the crowd before they can stop you. You're probably lucky that they didn't shoot you for that.`
				decline
			label no
			`	The voice gives a long hum but says no more. After a couple moments you hesitantly get up and, when the guards make no motion to prevent you, you leave.`
				decline
	on complete
		conversation
			`You guide the <ship> into the crowded spaceport of <planet>, narrowly avoiding a collision with one of a wing of armored-up Kvelqden rocketing out of the docking section.`
			choice
				`	(Seek out Myurej's contact.)`
					goto contact
				`	(Look around for yourself first.)`
			action
				"successors: ghosts suspicion" ++
			`	Exploring the visitor-accessible part of the station is an unusual experience - there's a striking contrast between the presence of all the advanced technologies of the Successors and the fact that so many of them are in such disrepair. You've seen Successor constructions that are hundreds or even thousands of years old in better condition than those here. You try to talk to a few of the Successors around here about Riiria, but they all quickly dismiss you, most without even saying a word.`
			`	Eventually you find your way to a shop of some sort - what looks like a gutted Myaede bolted to the station's structure and filled with displays of fabric and ship parts, all attended to by about a dozen small robots running on tracks on the ceiling. They follow you around like a school of fish; a couple of them have some ominous-looking apertures on their front. Suddenly, you hear the edited sound of Successor speech behind one of the displays of what looks like engine injectors. A small screen is projecting an image of a speaking Successor:`
			`	"...violence against Kaatrij is about us, too, siblings! The only one of the Houses who bothers t'give us the cant of an arm! For long the Old've wanted us gone entire, and believe me, this'll be the start'f it! Well, 'f they come for us, Riiria will make them bleed like I always do!" The transmission cuts out there, and with no further leads on Riiria's location, you decide to track down Myurej's contact.`
			label contact
			`	The Myurej merchant captain turns out to be almost a kilometer down the station's perimeter among some loading docks that station control apparently doesn't send unfamiliar ships to. They're directing several members of their crew to offload some crates - one of them has been dropped and has spilled out a collection of unfamiliar metal baubles.`
			choice
				`	"I'm Captain <first> <last>. Myurej sent me."`
					goto introduce
				`	"What are those things?"`
			`	"What cares thou? Thou'rt in the way, go off." They wave you away.`
			`	"Fine," you say. "Captain <first> <last>. Myurej sent me."`
			label introduce
			`	A wave of red and black bristles over their skin. "Of course," they say. "I should've guessed. Come to send me on some wild quest for some bit of finery, is it? Some golden child lost their favorite jewel?"`
			`	"Well, sort of," you say. "All I need from you is the location of Riiria. They stole something from Myurej that the House wants back."`
			`	"Predictable," they say. "Some blow to pride and they get a knave like thee to crawl in the mud."`
			choice
				`	"Just get to the point."`
					goto point
				`	"Why are you so angry?"`
			`	"No, not angry," they say. "Tired. They pay me to change my routes, I accept. They pay me to talk to the fools they send to me, I accept. They pay me to transport unknowables, and I lap it up. Thought the family connection would make things easier, but what dost thou do when that 'family's just after thee for thine use to them?" They let the colors of anger subside and gently rub three of their arms together.`
			label point
			`	"Fine. I hear that Riiria's hiding out among the hollow stations 'round our neighbor stars. They're good to hide if thou hast stolen something, brilliant hard to scan a sleeping ship among the broken spires. The northerly one... Vade-Osolaa-Kaska, I recall, 'tis a favorite spot for Riiria and their type. Were I thee, I'd crawl there first." The Successor pauses to look at one of the boxes being unloaded and makes an exasperated noise. "Not that being thee is aught I would prefer, mind."`
			choice
				`	"Thank you."`
				`	"Finally."`
			`	Color once again bristles over their skin, but only for a moment. "Now go 'fore the two of us are seen together," they say, and wave you away. You find your way back to your own ship and mark the nearby uninhabited station on your map.`

mission "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 2"
	landing
	priority
	name "Search <planet>"
	description "Following information from Myurej's contact, look for Riiria at <destination>."
	source Kasii-Tuur-Saqru
	destination Vade-Osolaa-Kaska
	to offer
		has "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 1: done"
	on complete
		conversation
			`You enter <planet>'s vast spaceport to find it almost deserted. There is, however, plenty of evidence to support your contact's suggestion. A number of empty but recently-opened cargo containers are strewn against one of the far walls of the space; beside one of them there's even a small cache of what looks like personal gear: a durable fabric pack, a small sidearm, even some packages of dried food. Someone must have left here in a hurry.`
			choice
				`	(Rummage through the pack.)`
				`	(Prepare to leave.)`
					goto end
			action
				"successors: ghosts suspicion" ++
			`	Inside you find, among the odds and ends of this Successor's belongings, a still-warm data-sphere. It springs to life as you touch it, relaying its most recent message:`
			`	"Riiria says the Houses shan't find us here, that they see these wretched hulks as icons'f their folly they daren't touch. They're right, I know, and yet I shudder most at thinking of that alien the Houses're so fond'f using. Riiria says fools're much more fearsome than the wise."`
			`	The message ends there, and you can't quite figure out how to access the rest of the data on the sphere, so you leave it be.`
			label end
			`	If Riiria isn't at this station, they might be at the other one to the south, so you head back to your ship and enter the coordinates on your map.`

mission "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 3"
	landing
	name "Continue the search"
	description "Having not found Riiria at <origin>, look for them at <destination>."
	source Vade-Osolaa-Kaska
	destination Myiara-Sola-Tej
	to offer
		has "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 2: done"
	on complete
		conversation
			`Not longer after you guide the <ship> through this station's docking aperture, you see parked on one of the disused landing pads a clearly unpowered Successor freighter. It's in poor condition; much of the hull armor has been removed and a hole has been bored down through the top right over the generator bay.`
			`	Fortunately, your ship's scanners are still able to identify its identification number, and you scramble for House Myurej's data-sphere to check it against the data Myurej provided you. This is the ship you were sent to find, you determine.`
			choice
				`	(Use your cargo scanner to identify its cargo.)`
					to display
						has "flagship attribute: cargo scan power"
				`	(Check its cargo yourself.)`
					goto self
			`	Unsurprisingly, the ship's cargo bays have been picked clean and whatever wedding gifts you have been sent to retrieve aren't here. The scanner is able to interface with an unshielded, barely-powered terminal inside the hulk, however, and relays to you the ship's most recent cargo manifest:`
			``
				goto manifest
			label self
			`	You disembark the <ship> and walk into the ripped-open cargo bay of the Ojde to confirm what already seems likely: every trace of the ship's cargo has been removed. You are able to access an independently-powered terminal inside the bay, however, and as it burbles to life, it shows you the ship's most recent cargo manifest:`
			``
			label manifest
			`		37 tons assorted gifts (common)`
			`		4 tons red gold jewelry`
			`		9 tons programmed water (for Council pools)`
			`		3 tons ceremonial weapons`
			`		9 tons rare animals (in stasis, require constant power supply)`
			`		16 tons high-pressure lux filters (require pressurized environment)`
			``
			`	Though most of the items don't tell you much, the last one seems like it could be a clue, and you press the terminal for details:`
			`	"House-built luxury filter units designed for undersea oxygen extraction and programming. Disperses mood-lightening particles with variable concentration. Must be kept in high-pressure environment to avoid damage. 8 million credits per unit."`
			branch mvk
				has "visited planet: Maspa-Viir-Kella"
			`	As you disconnect from the terminal, you think about any planets nearby that might fit the storage requirements of these filters, but nothing comes to mind. It looks like you'll have to check the nearby worlds manually.`
				goto end
			label mvk
			`	As you disconnect from the terminal, you think about any planets nearby that might fit the storage requirements of these filters, and one springs to mind: Maspa-Viir-Kella, an uninhabited world in the Osolaa-Uuoru system to the north. Landing there before was a challenge on account of the dense atmosphere; if the elusive Riiria is storing their spoils somewhere, that would be a good place for it.`
			label end


mission "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 3 Direct"
