mission "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 4"
	landing
	name "Defeat Riiria and return"
	description "If possible, retrieve the stolen wedding gifts from Riiria and return, gifts or not, to House Myurej at <destination>."
	source Maspa-Viir-Kella
	destination Raaqa-Kvelq-Ryuit
	to offer
		has "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 3: done"
	on offer
		conversation
			`The <ship>'s scanners spring to life not long after you enter <origin>'s atmosphere, pinging several unidentified ships in a nearby valley under the shroud of the thick clouds. As the winds buffet your ship, you check the scan readings you're receiving against the data that Myurej provided you, and they seem to match, at least for the largest of the vessels.`
			choice
				`	(Attack them while you have the element of surprise.)`
				`	(Try to negotiate.)`
			`	As you bring your own vessel closer, you are suddenly thrown off course by a strong gust of wind. Though you regain attitude control only a moment later, it's long enough for Riiria's ships to detect you and prepare for launch...`
				launch
	npc board
		government `People's Houses (Hostile)`
		personality staying target launching heroic
		system "Osolaa-Uuoru"
		ship "Ejniisde-Khora (Bombed)" "Riiria-i-Nnesan"
		conversation
			action
				log "Boarded Riiria's vessel, before being forced back by explosions from within that destroyed both Riiria's ship and the wedding gifts it presumably carried."
			`You bring your ship alongside Riiria's disabled vessel, careful to line up one of your airlocks with the ship's cargo hatch. As you walk through your vessel's interior to prepare to start cutting through the hatch, however, your ship is rocked by an explosion that seems like it comes from the airlock. Seconds later, another one goes off, and then another. Racing back to your ship's bridge, you detach from the detonating vessel just as another explosion rips through its cargo bay, no doubt destroying the precious cargo you've gone to so much effort to track down. This is going to be unpleasant to explain to House Myurej.`
				launch
	npc
		government `People's Houses (Hostile)`
		personality staying launching
		system "Osolaa-Uuoru"
		ship "Kvelqde-Khora" "Akja-o-Riiria"
		ship "Kvelqde-Khora" "Miti-o-Riiria"
		ship "Kvelqde-Khora" "Kaska-Kisiri"
		ship "Kvelqde-Khora" "Tesja-qii"
	on complete
		conversation
			`Traffic control directs you to a restricted part of the <planet> spaceport where the bare industry of the public areas gives way to Myurej ostentation. The <ship> settles down on a bronze-edged landing pad, and as you disembark, the armed and armored guards direct you to one of the adjoining buildings. Inside, the room you are led to is divided in much the same way as the previous time you met with House Myurej; a long black screen waves in front of you, and you wait for the voice to begin.`
			`	"We gave thee a simple task," it says. "Yet it seems even aught so basic eludes thee." They pause for a moment.`
			branch sioeora
				has "successors sioeora patron"
			`	"Mayhaps we should have learned from thy failure with Sioeora. Thou hast a habit, it seems to us."`
			label sioeora
			choice
				`	"I had nothing to do with Riiria's ship exploding."`
				`	"It seems to me like you're the one who needs to apologize. I was nearly killed!"`
					goto angry
				`	"I'm sorry."`
					goto grovel
			`	The screen ripples colorlessly. "What careth we? If we had sent another, would it still have been so?"`
				goto again
			label angry
			`	The screen ripples, dark and menacing. "Taking missions as these is what thou dost, is it not so? Is it common among lesser aliens as thee to berate one's clients for daring t'offer employ?"`
				goto again
			label grovel
			`	The screen ripples, lightless as tar. "We care little for thy apologies," says the voice, "but 'tis good that thou hast some cognizance of thine inability."`
			label again
			`	Suddenly, a wave of color springs across the screen. When the voice continues, there's something in it you can't quite place. "Thou couldst undo this failure for us, though, Captain. Find us some replacement for the things thou hast lost in thy folly. Thou couldst still earn our coin, our gratitude. Surely thou shouldst leap at this."`
			choice
				`	"Are you kidding me? I'm done with you."`
				`	"Fine. Tell me more."`
					goto more
			`	Something pulses in your ears, driving a momentary prick of pain deep into your head; you realize it's the translation device, picking up on something else in the room, some other bit of imperceptible sound murmuring in the background. The voice interrupts it. "We know what thou desirest, Captain," it says. "To be a part of the events to come, thou shalt need the backing of the Houses. None comes to pass in this space without our blessing. Cry and bark as thou must, thou still requirest us."`
			choice
				`	"Then tell me what you want, and I'll decide if it's worth my time."`
					goto more
				`	"What is that sound?"`
			`	You feel it again, this time much more subtle. You can't shake the feeling that it's like something has noticed you. "Do not distract thyself, Captain," says the voice, and the pressure lifts.`
			`	"Fine," you say, "just tell me what you want so I can decide if I want any more to do with you."`
			label more
			`	"Like before," the voice says, "when Sioeora asked their favor of thee, we've aught we wish to reclaim from the gyre of the Shroud. Nothing to upset thy delicate ethics - naught but trinkets from when the House was young. 'Twould make a fair consolation to us, and we would forgive thee, and thou wouldst know the beneficence of this House."`
			branch "not met solitude enforcers"
				not "Successors: Ghosts Aqrabe 7: offered"
			`	"Certain some drone warship isn't going to come after me as soon as I grab your trinkets?" you say, recalling the experience with House Aqrabe. This seems to catch the voice off guard, if only a little, and it takes a moment before it replies. "Any encounter thou hast met once before, thou shouldst surely be unafraid of facing again."`
			label "not met solitude enforcers"
			choice
				`	"I don't appreciate being treated as disposable."`
					to display
						has "Successors: Ghosts Aqrabe 7: offered"
				`	"All right, I'll do it. But you'd better hold up your end of the bargain."`
					goto yes
				`	"I'm done with this."`
					goto no
			`	"Thou'rt not a tool to be thrown away, Captain, but to be cultivated, polished to a gleam. We would not send thee to thy death - what benefits the House from that? Return to the spaceport here when thou'rt ready to begin thy task."`
				goto end
			label yes
			action
				log "Accepted an offer to take on an additional mission for House Myurej to retrieve Predecessor artifacts."
			`	"We shall," says the voice, "we always do. Return to the spaceport when thou'rt ready to begin."`
				goto end
			label no
			action
				log "Declined to take on additional mission for House Myurej to retrieve Predecessor artifacts. Can return to the Raaqa-Kvelq-Ryuit spaceport to accept it at a later date."
			`	"As thou sayst," says the voice. "When thou changest thy mind, return to the spaceport here to begin."`
			label end
			`	You exit the room with the screen and return to the landing pad with your ship.`

mission "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 5"
	priority
	name "Locate hidden vault"
	description "Enter House Myurej's hidden vault on <destination>, accompanied by Ijaset and two of House Myurej's soldiers."
	source Raaqa-Kvelq-Ryuit
	destination Kella-Uuoru-Sossa
	passengers 3
	to offer
		has "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 4: done"
	on offer
		conversation
			`You wait around in the spaceport in a low, columned area. Circular depressions in the ground hold pools of water, and occasionally a Successor will come along and slither into one for a few minutes before getting on with their business. After a while, you are met by what must be an envoy of House Myurej, a tall Successor wearing the same colors as their military officers, albeit in a somewhat less martial outfit. Two soldiers flank them. "Captain <last>?" they say. "How excellent to meet thee."`
			choice
				`	"Yes. And you are?"`
					goto hello
				`	"You seem more polite than the rest of Myurej."`
			`	"I'm not sure what thou mean'st. I harbor no ill will to thee, for certain."`
			label hello
			`	They quirk their head at you for a moment before speaking again. "I am Ijaset. I contribute to Myurej's efforts t'explore beyond the wormhole."`
			`	"And your friends?" you say, gesturing to the soldiers.`
			`	Blue spots run over Ijaset's skin; you realize it's the first time you've seen a color display by a member of Myurej. "They are here to assure the success of our task."`
			label questions
			choice
				`	"Can you tell me more about our mission?"`
					goto mission
				`	"What exactly are your efforts to explore beyond the wormhole?"`
					to display
						not "Successors: efforts"
					goto efforts
				`	"Seems like the guards are more of an implied threat."`
					to display
						not "Successors: threat"
					goto threat
			label efforts
			action
				set "Successors: efforts"
			`	Ijaset relaxes and leans against a column, looking over the nearest pool. "Probes, for the most part. They're small enough to bring to speed with a planetary coilgun, and after a couple of years go by, we get some data back. In years past, some of the nearer stars lay more connected than they are now, and we could send whole ships. But never as far as Myurej now requests us go."`
				goto questions
			label threat
			action
				set "Successors: threat"
			`	The soldiers shuffle in place a little bit, and Ijaset stiffens. "The Houses need not threaten thee, <last>. They get what they want without such things; they've had eons to learn to do that."`
				goto questions
			label mission
			action
				clear "Successors: animal"
				clear "Successors: others"
			`	"Myurej seeks to send us to <planet>," they say. "I've been fashioned with the location and key to a hidden vault 'pon the surface. Inside, Myurej's Predecessors kept a bevy of things ineffable, but we need not retrieve much. Today, all they ask of us is a collection of jewelry contained within." They pause and let a collection of colors emerge over them. A gentle breeze whistles through the columns. "The smallest things presage the grandest journeys," they say. "Let us go to thy craft and begin with haste."`
				accept
	on complete
		conversation
			`You set down the <ship> on the outskirts of one of the smaller cities on <planet>. The buildings are in remarkably good condition for having stood here thousands of years - most of them, at least, because several have been leveled by weapons fire. The entire easternmost quarter of the city has been reduced to rubble; twisted spars of metal rise up where buildings once did and stone plazas lie shattered in the dust and sun.`
			`	Ijaset leads you, along with the two Myurej soldiers, to an area that's a curious reflection of the columned pool area of the Myurej spaceport, though here all the water has long since evaporated. The one here is larger, too, and as you walk through the forest of white pillars, it becomes more and more difficult to see back to your ship in the distance.`
			`	Eventually, Ijaset stops on the edge of one of the depressions. "Tis here," they say, emotionless, and point directions to the two guards. They check something against a datapad they produce from their clothing, and then glide over to one of the columns, extending three arms to feel around the circumference of it. Shortly after, something clicks, and a rumbling suddenly starts below you, growing louder and louder until it stops and an aperture opens in the middle of the depression. A tunnel yawns deep into the ground.`
			choice
				`	"That's a long way down."`
					goto down
				`	"Why put a vault in a place like this?"`
			`	Ijaset hums. "'Twas once a reserved quarter for the highborn of Myurej, this. Secret to those outside, but known to those who weren't. Then, as now, knowledge was a matter of position."`
			label down
			`	You go to look over the edge, and Ijaset joins you. "We should expect a long journey," they say. "'Twas meant to be shielded from just such a bombardment as came to pass."`
			`	The four of you make your way down the tunnel, which seems to go down into the planet for kilometers. The dark metal walls grow warm to the touch, and the slippery floor proves more treacherous for you than for the Successors - you have to catch yourself on the rail several times. Eventually you come to an enormous spherical room, large enough that the far wall fades into darkness even as a shaft above you lets in an impossibly-penetrating beam of sunlight. Ringing the walls are thousands upon thousands of circular insets, each one many meters in diameter. Their centers have a glossy sheen, as if they are slightly wet.`
			choice
				`	"I had no idea the Houses had this much."`
				`	"We can't be here just for jewelry, can we?"`
			`	"Myurej had dozens of these vaults," Ijaset says. "Most not here, not on the homeworld. Ships, weapons, great riches grown in the heart of stars... all should be preserved, lest the Quarg or some other despoilers have come to empty them. Today we come for trinkets, so tomorrow we can come for the rest."`
			choice
				`	"Let's just focus on what we're here for."`
					goto next
				`	"With the contents of a vault like this, any of the Houses could dominate the others, couldn't they?"`
			`	One of the soldiers says something to Ijaset, loud enough for you to hear, but in a dialect your translation device doesn't pick up. They nod. "Kaatrij wounded, the People's Houses in disarray, even fair Myurej soon to be drawn ever closer to Chydiyi. 'Tis a time of change and the uncertain. With the contents of a vault as this, any of the Houses could make their own certainty."`
			label next
			`	Ijaset confers with their datapad and leads the three of you a couple of degrees along the great room's circumference, stopping in front of one of the insets. They produce from a pocket a gilded data-sphere that they press into its face, and you watch as the golden strands encircling it lay themselves out on the front of the surface, forming a fractal web of glittering metal. When they finally stop moving, the whole face of the inset liquefies, gold and all. Behind it lies a deep circular room stacked with elegant wooden boxes. The four of you enter and Ijaset collects a few small items, most no larger than your hand. They give most to the soldiers, but reserve three or four to carry themself.`
			`	"That's it?" you say.`
			`	"Indeed," says Ijaset. "A shame to leave the rest, I know, but if it's stayed a thousand years, it shall bear another one."`
			`	You all retreat from the vault room; Ijaset first, followed by you and then the soldiers. As their last trailing arm slides over the threshold, the face of the vault reforms as quickly as it had melted, the golden strands retract back to the data-sphere, and the whole room is left as it was before. As you prepare to go back up, however, something sharp pings in your ear.`
			choice
				`	"What is that?"`
				`	"Did you hear that?"`
			`	Ijaset looks over at you with a shade of concern on their face. They open their mouth, but nothing understandable comes out - just the same sharply flowing language you heard from the Successors before you acquired the translation device. Then, a second later, there's another sharp feeling and their words are reshaped. "...thine ears? Canst thou... now, I see it. We must leave now, <last>."`
			`	The vault is shaken by the deep and distant sound of something breaking. Your translation device seems to be mostly back to normal, but something isn't quite right, as if it's trying to reshape some deep environmental noise in the background. It's hard to concentrate. There's another blast of sound, and you follow the three Successors back up the tunnel. It seems even longer now than it did before.`
			`	Just as you emerge into the sunlight, something slams into the ground in the distance and you are thrown onto the stone. As you get back up, you hear Ijaset shouting a word that your translation device can't translate. A couple of seconds later, you see what it was that knocked you down: a brilliant stream of plasma illuminates the sky as a hypervelocity projectile strikes one of the buildings in the city. The air stinks of ozone.`
			choice
				`	(Run for your ship.)`
					goto run
				`	(Radio for your ship to come pick you up.)`
					to display
						has "flagship attribute: shields"
						has "flagship crew"
			`	You quickly transmit new landing coordinates for the <ship> and its repulsors kick up the dust as another building in the city is leveled. As it nears the columned area, the orbital weapon fires again, this time targeting your ship. Its shields flash as they shatter the projectile, the shards of which tear through a swath of columns to your left. As you dash aboard the landing ramp with the Successors right behind you, another impact knocks your vessel to the side and you prepare to fly into orbit while your ship's shields still hold.`
				launch
			label run
			`	You run back through the field of columns as the bombardment continues. Some of the impacts feel like they're getting closer the farther you run, but eventually you make it back to where you landed the <ship> and hurry inside with Myurej's agents right behind you. As you make your way to the bridge, another impact strikes dangerously close to your landing area, and you prepare to fly into orbit while you still can.`
				launch

mission "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 6"
	landing
	priority
	name "Flee back to Successor space"
	description "Escape the warships attacking you and regroup in Successor space."
	source Kella-Uuoru-Sossa
	destination Uuoru-Veldt-Stir
	passengers 3
	to offer
		has "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 5: done"
	npc evade
		ship "Queru, Luminous Gaze" "Kis, Lamenting 9-3"
		ship "Queru, Luminous Gaze" "Maki, Recalling 11-2"
		government "Solitude Enforcer"
		personality waiting heroic nemesis unconstrained vindictive
		on kill
			set "Successors: Ghosts Queru transmission"
			dialog "As the second drone ship explodes it transmits some data to your vessel. It cannot be deciphered at this time."
	on enter "Myruet-Kvelq"
		"successors: ghosts met solitude enforcers" ++
		"successors: ghosts suspicion" ++
		dialog `Ijaset instructs you to land on the uninhabited world here to hand over the Predecessor artifacts.`
	on complete
		payment 400000
		log "Handed off the jewelry House Myurej wanted after being chased out of Predecessor space by a pair of long-ranged warships."
		conversation
			`The <ship> comes to rest on the gentle hills of <planet> next to an unassuming-looking Myaede freighter. Though the air here is too rarefied for you to breathe, Ijaset and the two Successor soldiers seem to handle it well enough, transferring their haul of little boxes over to the freighter. As you watch from your ship, you think you recognize the captain of the freighter as the same merchant captain you spoke to back on Kasii-Tuur-Saqru. The two soldiers board the freighter, while Ijaset returns to your ship to speak with you.`
			`	"Well done, <last>," they say. "Thou kept thy calm very well."`
			choice
				`	"Do you know anything about those ships that attacked us?"`
				`	"Why the secrecy?"`
					goto secrecy
			action
				"successors: ghosts suspicion" ++
			`	Ijaset lets out a long sigh, accompanied by muted color. "Ancient warships, it would seem, built by our Predecessors in their day. There's aught familiar about them, but they were not Myurej's, if that concerns thee. Something..." Crimson sparkles dot their skin, reminiscent of anger or frustration, "T'weren't some grand heirlooms like the Houses smuggled 'cross the wormhole, at least. I suspect they were waiting for us, or some like us, to disturb the lost worlds' esoterica."`
			choice
				`	"Why all the secrecy?"`
					goto secrecy
			label secrecy
			`	Ijaset leans against a bulkhead. "I think Myurej wishes to place our trinkets in the arms of someone who knows not what they are. They do not trust thee, and canst thou blame them?"`
			choice
				`	"I suppose not."`
				`	"Yes I can, actually."`
			`	"'Tis fair, <last>," they say. "I should inform thee that thy agreed-upon fee of <payment> should be released to thee soon. As for Myurej's favor, 'tisn't aught I can convey to thee myself. I suspect they'll wish to contact thee on their own time to decide upon thy status with the House. Until then, I'll take my leave of thee. If we meet again, may it be on pleasant terms."`

mission "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 7"
	landing
	name "Return to Myurej"
	description "Return to House Myurej at <destination> to find out if they have anything more for you."
	source
		attributes successor
		not attributes uninhabited
	destination Raaqa-Kvelq-Ryuit
	to offer
		has "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 6: done"
		random < 40
	on offer
		conversation
			`Shortly after you land at the spaceport here, you receive a message delivered via data-sphere:`
			`	Captain <first> <last>. House Myurej asks that thou join us on <planet> as soon as thou mayst, so that we may conclude our business with thee.`
			`	As soon as it finishes playing, it adds a waypoint to your ship's map.`
				accept

mission "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 8"
	landing
	name "Deliver wedding supplies"
	description "A dockworker at <origin> has directed you to deliver <tons> of wedding supplies for House Myurej to <destination>."
	source Raaqa-Kvelq-Ryuit
	destination Iyra-Ijasa-Iret
	cargo "Wedding supplies" 5
	to offer
		has "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 7: done"
	on offer
		conversation
			`Once again traffic control directs you to the reserved portion of the <origin> spaceport with the bronze-trimmed landing pads. You are met outside by a somewhat stressed-looking dockworker who brightens up considerably when they see you.`
			`	"Of course, of course," they say, "we've been waiting for thee! A House transport to <planet> of supplies for the wedding, yes?"`
			choice
				`	"Excuse me?"`
				`	"I was suppose to meet someone here, I think."`
			`	The worker checks their datapad, looking back and forth between it and you before they once again announce with confidence that you are supposed to transport <tons> of wedding supplies to <planet> for the upcoming Myurej wedding.`
			choice
				`	"Well, get them loaded, I suppose."`
					accept
				`	"I'll come back later."`
					defer
	on complete
		"successors: ghosts houses dealt with" ++
		set "successors: ghosts dealt with myurej"
		log "Spoke with Khiajsore, a scion of House Myurej, at an underwater venue where an inter-House wedding is set to occur."
		conversation
			`The <ship> settles down in one of the metal bubbles of the <planet> spaceport and before long, as the ground crew is unloading your ship's cargo, a pair of House Myurej's soldiers comes to lead you through the facility. They take you to an elevator outside of the spaceport's public area; you step in, and a few seconds after it begins moving, it clears the bulk of the spaceport complex and shows you a fantastic view of the planet's ocean as it descends deeper into the water. Unfortunately you're on the wrong side of the planet to see the bioluminscent algal streams of the "Ribbons of Iret," but even the relatively dark sea is impressive in its scale and in the vastness of the underwater infrastructure the Successors have built within it.`
			`	Eventually the elevator nestles into a complex on the seafloor, and the two guards guide you through a number of transparent halls to a large central area. Fish swim above you, schooling behind a circular oculus. Another Successor approaches from one of the side corridors, and it is immediately apparent that this is one of Myurej's scions - they are draped in enough red gold and jewels that it's a wonder they can hold their body upright. When they speak, it's not the voice you heard behind the waving screen before, but one that's smoother and more inquisitive.`
			`	"Captain, captain," they say, "thou, Captain, who hast brought us such lovely glitterings with such fine loyalty. And through such perilous straits, I hear as well? The knave Riiria, the fearsome guardians of the Shroud... I could not bear to keep myself from seeing thee in the flesh, the flesh that holds all this surpassing strength!" Their adornments rattle as they gesture, prodding the air gently.`
			choice
				`	"I hope I live up to your expectations."`
					goto flirty
				`	"It seems like a lot of effort for some little trinkets."`
					goto unamused
				`	"And you are?"`
			`	The scion fans their arms gently. "Myurej M- Khiajsore. A cousin of the one who spoke to thee earlier, whom thou shalt recall."`
				goto next
			label flirty
			`	"Quite so!" the scion says. "They say a - what is it - a 'biped fever' runs through the people since thou arriv'st, that all at once all the worlds clamor for stories of artful, noble humans in the heyday of our Predecessors. I did not see the appeal at first, but by thy actions and seeing thee now... there's a certain strange elegance to the few arms, thine incomplete symmetry." They hum briefly. "But forgive me, that's not what we're here for, thou or I." They fan their arms in a fluid motion. "Myurej M- Khiajsore. I'm a cousin of the one who spoke to thee earlier, behind the veil."`
				goto next
			label unamused
			`	The scion extends a gilded arm, shaking the myriad piercings and bits of jewelry upon it as if to contemplate them. "Oh, thou think'st me materialistic, mayhaps? Yet precious things are only made precious by the pain of acquiring them. The jewels thou didst bring back from the Shroud have already earned their own stories... as the beginning of a grand project of restoration, maybe, and at least as something totally unique." They hum with satisfaction. "And yet, 'tis not what we're here for, thou or I." They fan their arms in acknowledgment. "Myurej M- Khiajsore. A cousin of the one who spoke to thee earlier, behind the veil."`
			label next
			`	Khiajsore motions for you to join them on a stroll through the complex, the guards staying several meters behind. Plants with saffron-colored flowers line water-filled channels on the floor; their heads follow the two of you as you walk and slither along.`
			branch patron
				has "successor kaatrij patron"
			`	"'Tis about our friends at House Kaatrij," they say.`
				goto kaatrij
			label patron
			`	"'Tis about our friends at House Kaatrij," they say. "Thou'rt a friend to them, too, I know. Mirth runs up me every time I see Riijaaora, knowing what thou deni'dst them. 'Twere always an ill-mooded sort."`
			label kaatrij
			`	One of the saffron plants bursts into a cloud of pollen that forms a film on the surface of the channel's water. "I've known Kaatrij for long now, all their love for secrecy and understatement. I think, dear captain, that they are wounded and volatile, and I know," they say, sparkling with energy, "that someone else behind the scenes moves all their pieces round and round and is, for now, winning this grand game."`
			choice
				`	"I'm not ready to jump to conclusions."`
				`	"Why not Myurej?"`
					goto myurej
			`	Mirth speckles the scion's skin. "Dost thou seek to add wisdom to thy list of virtues? I speak of this to thee so that thou mightst appreciate the circumstances in which thou earn'st our favor, in which we shall deliver it. Soon enough, as we the Houses promise thee ships and technologies, there will be a new day of chaos, and we shall promise thee these things as our inhibitions wane and our judgment warps in the glare of this new light."`
				goto stop
			label myurej
			`	Khiajsore hums again. It almost sounds like a piece of music; nothing you're familiar with, of course. "Myurej, Myurej, Myurej," they say. "For the rest here, Myurej is the state, but for those of us within it, Myurej is family. Were we the ones making up this crisis, I surely wouldn't tell thee, discreet as thou mayst have proven thyself." Jovial pastels color the scion's gilded body. "Soon enough, we the Houses shall promise thee all sorts of trinkets - ships and technologies - as our inhibitions fade in this ongoing disorder. Our judgment will be turned to new aims."`
			label stop
			`	Khiajsore stops in a circular room where the flowers have spread out to colonize the space, dusting the air and water alike with their bright pollen. "I wish to invite thee to our wedding, Captain. Not mine!" they chuckle, "but Myurej's. 'Twill take place here, beneath the waves, as our kind once began in eons past. And it shall be a gathering of the Houses, of everyone of import. If thou hast made allies of others, as thou hast of us, there would be the place to petition thy case to all assembled. And," they add with a bright tone, "I do hope thou wilt enjoy the show."`
			`	They glide over to one of the walls and pluck one of the flowers before returning and offering it to you. The golden bloom rotates to face you as you take it from them, opening wide to reveal its bright interior. "Farewell now." they say, "The complex here shall meet thy needs, if thou requirest rest or aught else before thou must depart. May next we meet be as delightful as today, Captain." Khiajsore splays their arms to you once again, and they are joined by their two escorts as they slither down one of the complex's corridors.`
			`	When, a while later, you take the elevator back up to the planet's surface, you cannot help but notice how similar the window into the dark ocean is to Myurej's shimmering black screen.`

