			"successors: ghosts suspicion" >= 4
			"successors: ghosts houses dealt with" >= 2
		has "event: successors: ghosts seineq attacked"
	cargo "Scientific equipment" 10
	passengers 3
	on offer
		conversation
			branch kaatrij
				has "successors kaatrij patron"

			`Waiting in the spaceport here as you arrive is a trio of Successors comprising two guards and one other individual who wears a black, cocoon-like outfit with lots of pockets. Both of the guards bear the insignia of House Kaatrij.`
			`	The black-draped individual bows gently to you as green sparkles dot their skin. "Captain <first> <last>?" they say. When you indicate affirmatively, they continue. "I am Saajret, of Somber Sejra, an envoy of the noble scions of House Kaatrij. Kaatrij hopes that thou mightst do us a boon."`
				goto questions

			label kaatrij
			`Waiting in the spaceport here as you arrive are a trio of Successors, two guards and one other individual who you recognize as Saajret, of Somber Sejra. Kaatrij's archivist looks different from the last time you saw them; their outfit is wrapped up more tightly and the colors of their face seem muted and subdued.`
			`	Saajret bows to you gently, green and reddish tones swirling on their skin. "Captain <first> <last>," they say, "whose patience I have tested thoroughly, it would seem. Kaatrij sends me to ask of thee a boon to us."`

			label questions
			choice
				`	"Why haven't I heard from you since the incident?"`
					to display
						has "successors kaatrij patron"
					goto silence
				`	"What sort of 'boon?'"`
					goto boon
				`	"Why me?"`

			label me
			`	"Thou'rt earning thyself a reputation for efficiency and discretion," Saajret says. "And Kaatrij has need of both. Some scientific equipment here must return to the homeworld, ideally with haste. Canst thy craft serve?"`
				goto offer

			label boon
			`	"Thy reputation for professionalism seems well-earned, Captain," they say. "Some scientific equipment stored here must return to the homeworld with haste. Canst thy craft serve?"`
				goto offer

			label silence
			`	Saajret hums, colors continuing to swim over their body. Eventually, they speak. "In the wake of Kaatrij's wound, our suspicion of others was great and wide. And thou wert included in this, for these incidents came only soon after thy arrival. Some believe thou play'd some part in this, some do not." They pause for a moment, running their eyes over you. "'Tis the latter faction that offers thee this opportunity: some equipment here must return to the homeworld. A chance to demonstrate thy benevolence, mayhaps?"`

			label offer
			choice
				`	"All right. I assume the House is paying?"`
					goto accepted
				`	"I don't want to get involved in this."`

			`	"Very well," Saajret says. "'Tis thy own choice, after all."`
				decline

			label accepted
			`	"Of course," Saajret says. "I will see the items are loaded forthwith."`
				accept

	on decline
		dialog "successor ghosts story failed"

	on fail
		dialog "successor ghosts story failed"

	on complete
		payment 40000
		conversation
			branch "visited before"
				or
					has "successors kaatrij patron"
					has "visited planet: Raaqa-Puan-Uuoru"

			`You've heard <planet> described by outsiders as an insular and well-guarded world, but neither of those prepared you for how strikingly quiet it is. The rainy spaceport seems almost deserted, the loudest sound almost always the pattering of heavy drops on the sail-like projections overhead, only occasionally interrupted by a soft-spoken announcement about an incoming ship landing or departing. None of the Successors you transported give any indication about whether this is typical or just a result of Kaatrij's recent incidents.`
				goto paid

			label "visited before"
			`The <planet> spaceport is caught in the midst of a gentle rainstorm. The loudest sound you hear during the time you spend there is the patter of the heavy drops overhead and the occasional whirring of the machinery the dockworkers use to unload your cargo.`

			label paid
			`	Saajret meets with you on the landing pad, informing you that you've been credited <payment> by the House for your services. Before leaving, they ask you to return to the spaceport this evening to meet with them.`



mission "Successors: Ghosts 6"
	name "Visit <planet> again"
	description "Saajret, of Somber Sejra has been instructed by House Kaatrij to scan the wildlife on <destination>, which must be of interest to multiple of the High Houses."
	source "Raaqa-Puan-Uuoru"
	destination "Raaqa-Uur-Kaav"
	passengers 1
	to offer
		has "Successors: Ghosts 5: done"
	on offer
		conversation
			`The black-shrouded Saajret meets you back at the spaceport as the sun is setting, joining you in a lobby area looking out on a landing pad for Kaatrij's military ships. As they start to speak, a pair of Veusaden hover to the ground in the distance, their repulsor thrusters kicking into the air drops of the everpresent rain.`
			`	"I've managed to convince Kaatrij that thou mightst be helpful to us in one more task," they say. "As the situation develops, they now agree thou'rt too substantive to deny all dialog. Dost thou remember thy prior visit to <planet>, wherein thou didst confront the Kijran?"`
			choice
				`	"Yes."`
				`	"It was hard to forget."`
			branch kaatrij
				has "successors kaatrij patron"

			action
				log "People" "Saajret, of Somber Sejra" "Saajret, of Somber Sejra is an archivist, among other things, for the Successor High House Kaatrij."
			`	"My role here is... something of an archivist," Saajret says, "collecting and ordering information, items, records, of our Predecessors 'fore we left that period behind. Kaatrij believes certain data about the creatures on the old homeworld would be of use to them, and since thou now providest them the opportunity," they say, spreading their arms in a wide gesture, "Kaatrij is willing to compensate thee for taking me there to scan them."`
				goto choices

			label kaatrij
			`	"I'm an archivist, as I told thee before," Saajret continues. "Kaatrij believes certain data about the creatures there would be of use to them and, since thou now providest them the opportunity, shall compensate thee for taking me there to scan them."`

			label choices
			choice
				`	"In the wake of an attack, Kaatrij's interest is in scanning plants and animals? I don't buy it."`
					to display
						"successors: ghosts suspicion" >= 6
					goto suspicious

				`	"Last time I went the wildlife wasn't very friendly."`
					to display
						not "Successors FC3: friend to animals"
					goto scared

				`	"All right."`
					to display
						has "Successors FC3: friend to animals"
					goto yes

				`	"I have no interest in going back there."`

			`	Saajret hums. "After thy prior experience, I wonder'd if that would be the case. Very well," they say. "I'll bid thee farewell, then."`
				decline

			label yes
			`	"So readily accepted?" Saajret says, more than a little surprised. "Perhaps thy prior experience was not as fearful as I thought. In that case, I shall ready myself to leave and meet thee at thy craft."`
				accept

			label scared
			`	"Indeed not," Saajret says, humming. "Thou shalt not be expected to face them again, if that concerns thee. The scans I mean to take are not invasive and would not arouse the fury of the Kijran-Khora, but thou'rt needed for naught but transportation there and back."`
				goto "final choice"

			label suspicious
			branch "kaatrij kijran"
				has "successors kaatrij patron"

			`	Saajret laughs, a quiet ruk-ruk sound that doesn't seem very mirthful. "Perhaps not," they say. "These creatures are important to the House nonetheless. They were important enough to House Sioeora to pay thee to steal, were they not?" They pause, continuing more quietly. "In their own way they are valuable to Kaatrij," they finally add. "What say'st thou to the House's offer?"`
				goto "final choice"

			label "kaatrij kijran"
			`	Saajret laughs, a quiet ruk-ruk sound that doesn't seem very mirthful. "'Twas the Kaatrij of old that engineered them, was it not? Is it not sensible that they would be important to the House, worthy of a cast gaze even in a fraught time?" They pause for a moment, a swirl of indeterminate colors on their face. "What say'st thou to the House's offer?" they finally say.`
				goto "final choice"

			label "final choice"
			choice
				`	"All right, I'll do it."`
				`	"I'm still not willing to go back."`
					decline

			`	"Kaatrij will be pleased," says Saajret. "I shall ready myself to leave and meet thee then at thy craft."`
				accept

	on complete
		conversation
			`	You land your ship on the outskirts of the same facility you visited with Sieasej in the past; it looks much the same, though now many of the green plants have turned various shades of yellow and orange as the seasons have changed. Saajret meets you in your ship's cockpit, now dressed in a slightly different black, well-pocketed outfit. They carry a device with a rotating drum in one of their arms, probably some sort of scanner.`
			`	"I shall keep in contact with thy craft," they say, "though I foresee no problems in my expedition. Expect me back about three hours hence."`
			`	As they leave, you are left with little to do but wait.`
			choice
				`	(Assess your ship's systems.)`
					goto inside
				`	(Look around outside.)`

			branch "friend to animals"
				has "Successors FC3: friend to animals"

			`	The remarkably peaceful vista conceals a feeling of unease; in the distance, you see cuts in a couple of trees, their bark leaking sap from a wound surely left by a serrated antenna. You spy what you recognize as a Kijra-riita flitting between trees; it drains a flower of nectar on a shrub and bats a twig full of dried leaves, knocking a few to the ground. Perhaps it's the same one you encountered the last time you visited.`
				goto saajret

			label "friend to animals"
			`	It's a remarkably peaceful vista and only becomes more so as the day wears into late afternoon and the autumn color is amplified by the golden sunlight. In the distance you see what you recognize as a Kijra-riita flitting between trees; it laps nectar from a flower on a shrub and playfully bats at a twig full of dried leaves, knocking a few to the ground. Perhaps it's the same one you released the last time you visited.`
				goto saajret

			label inside
			branch "killed riiria"
				or
					has "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 4: done"
					has "Successors: Ghosts Myurej 4: active"

			`	You check over the <ship>'s various internal systems, making sure its power couplings are operating within normal parameters and taking a long moment to admire its jump drive, which hums away inside its housing, inscrutable as always.`
				goto saajret

			label "killed riiria"
			action
				"successors: ghosts suspicion" ++
			`	You check over the <ship>'s various internal systems, and discover a mysterious anomaly in one of the power consumption logs, though it's hard to track down what caused it or where it was located. Regardless, the anomaly resolved itself some time ago.`

			label saajret
			`	Saajret soon returns as they promised, apparently unharmed. They unload their equipment in the quarters you set aside for them before returning to you in the cockpit. "It went without incident," they say, a shade of satisfaction on their skin. As they turn to go away, they catch themself, turning back around with a bit of trepidation. "I may never get this chance again, so I'll speak now: I've a personal request to beg of thee. There's another world within the Shroud where in the past my ancestors resided. 'Fore we return to Kaatrij, I'd long to see it for myself. I'd pay thee for the diversion, of course."`
			choice
				`	"Sure, I'll take you."`
					goto helped
				`	"Sorry, you'll have to figure something else out."`
			`	Saajret struggles to keep their disappointment from showing. "Very well," they manage to say before leaving.`
				goto end

			label helped
			action
				set "Successors: Ghosts Helped Saajret"
			`	Saajret keeps their composure for a second before a faint pink color creeps up their face and arms. "My thanks to thee, Captain," they say. "The world is Osolaa-Val-Mavra; I'll give thee its place."`

			label end
			`	With nothing left to do here, you prepare to leave.`



mission "Successors: Ghosts 7a"
	transition
	clearance
	name "Detour to Osolaa-Val-Mavra"
	description "Saajret has asked to visit <stopovers> as a personal favor, before returning home to <planet>."
	stopover "Osolaa-Val-Mavra"
	destination "Raaqa-Puan-Uuoru"
	passengers 1
	to offer
		has "Successors: Ghosts 6: done"
		has "Successors: Ghosts Helped Saajret"
	on stopover
		log "Took Saajret to the Predecessor planet Osolaa-Val-Mavra. They visited an abandoned city on the surface where an ancestor of theirs once lived, retrieving from it a data-sphere and a small wooden box."
		conversation
			`You set the <ship> on one of the landing terraces of the planet's equatorial trench, near a location that Saajret indicates. The spot provides a dizzying view: snowflakes from a cloud overhead drift over ledges and deserted balconies before falling kilometers down into the abyss below. Saajret joins you by the airlock, now wrapped warmly in a shiny silver outfit with a collar of small ribbons that stream in the breeze.`
			`	"What is this place?" you ask.`
			`	A blue tone makes its way over Saajret's face. "'Twas an arc of homes and shops before they were abandoned," they say. A couple of snowflakes land on their skin and their arms wriggle against the white ground. "Thou may'st join me if thou desirest. Kaatrij demands no secrecy from us here."`
			choice
				`	(Go with them.)`
				`	(Stay.)`
					goto stay
			`	The two of you make your way through the abandoned streets. You are struck by how well-preserved everything is; more than those of any other Predecessor world, the buildings here seem only temporarily vacant, as if the two of you had merely caught the city on a day with everyone missing. A trio of little cleaning robots run around the rim of a fountain, polishing away the snow before it even has time to melt in the sun.`
			`	Saajret follows their own path, periodically checking what must be a map on a datapad they carry. Occasionally their skin will erupt in color as they see something that interests them, but they never stay distracted for long. Eventually the two of you arrive in an elegant square of organic buildings; Saajret checks their map a few times before declaring, "Here we are."`
			choice
				`	"And where is 'here'?"`
				`	"It's a pretty spot."`
				`	(Stay silent.)`
					goto building

			`	"An ancestor of mine lived here briefly," they say. "One of import in the last days of House Sejra. But when they lived here, all that was still to come."`

			label building
			`	Saajret walks inside the largest building, entering a code onto a spherical terminal beside the door. You move to go after them, but they hold out an arm to stop you. "This last part, I would prefer to go alone," they say. They point to a high bench outside.`
			`	They stay inside for about half an hour; you watch the snow fall on the square and the terraces. When Saajret returns, they are carrying a data-sphere and a small wooden box that they carry cradled in one of their arms. There's a color on their face you can't quite place.`
			choice
				`	"Are you ready to return?"`
				`	"What did you get?"`
					goto nosy
			`	They hum. "Yes, I have what I came for," they say, "thanks to thine indulgence of me. I shan't forget that."`
				goto end

			label nosy
			`	They hum. "One thing I had hoped for and another I had dreaded. So often those two go arm-in-arm, do they not?" The color on their face fades. "I have what I came for," they say. "My thanks to thee for indulging me in this."`
				goto end

			label stay
			`	Saajret splays their arms as farewell and tells you to expect them back before nightfall. You look over your ship's systems, take in the views, and watch the snow clump in the joints of the <ship>'s hull.`
			`	A couple of hours later, Saajret returns. They carry in their arms a data-sphere and a small wooden box, intricately carved. "I have all I came for, I believe," they tell you, and there's a color on their face you can't quite place. "My thanks," they say, "for indulging me."`

			label end
			`	The two of you pack up your things and prepare for departure.`
	on complete
		log "Saajret told a story about the hunting practices of the elusive self-camouflaging Kijran-Khora. These infiltrated House Kaatrij's bases long in the past. They suggested someone might do something similar."
		payment 220000
		conversation "saajret returns"
		event "successors: ghosts cloak prompt delay" 30
		"Successors: Ghosts Saajret Forgiveness" -- # Decreases as Saajret learns more about their personal past.



