conversation "saajret returns"
	`	Your ship once again glides into the <planet> spaceport, slipping beneath a dense layer of early-morning fog. Saajret meets you just outside, informing you the data they were sent to collect has already been transmitted and thanking you for your help.`
	branch helped
		has "Successors: Ghosts Helped Saajret"
	`	They tell you to expect a deposit of <payment> from House Kaatrij.`
		goto secret

	label helped
	`	They tell you to expect a deposit of 140000 credits from House Kaatrij and hand over a small chip containing 80000 additional credits.`

	label secret
	`	As Saajret watches a dockworker fitting a fuel hose to the <ship>'s side, something changes in their demeanor and a glint of almost furious orange sparks on their skin. "Captain," they say. "I'm told that thou'st experienced for thyself the hunting practices of the dread Kijran-Khora."`
	choice
		`	"I beg your pardon?"`
		`	"A little too closely, actually."`
	`	They continue, the color continuing to sparkle on their skin. "Beautiful beasts, aren't they? Truly aspirational; adept at camouflage, hiding themselves beyond all but the most scrutinizing gaze before closing in on their quarry. In the early days of Kaatrij, when the Kijran were still new, some particularly well-cloaked ones slipped into a weather-control tower. Perhaps," they say, "one might learn from their example, were there somewhere notable one wished to go." They cast their gaze upward, where the shimmering dots of planets above peek through the clouds.`
	choice
		`	"Why are you telling me this?"`
		`	"Are you trying to tell me something?"`
			goto foolish
	`	The sparkle of color on their skin dies down and they look at you with mirth in their eyes. "I'm an archivist," they say. "I adore a good story."`
		goto end

	label foolish
	`	The sparkle of color on their face intensifies for a moment before dying out. "Naught but an archivist's foolish games," they say.`

	label end
	`	They look over at the spaceport again. "Till again we meet, <first> <last>."`



mission "Successors: Ghosts Cloak Prompt"
	landing
	name "Investigate <planet>"
	description "Saajret's cryptic message may have been suggesting a way to more closely investigate House Kaatrij's hidden base on <planet>. Try to bypass the blockade by using a ship that can cloak."
	destination "Qasa-Sija-Iri"
	source
		attributes successor
		not attributes uninhabited crime
	to offer
		has "event: successors: ghosts cloak prompt delay"
		not "Successors: Ghosts 8: offered"
	on offer
		conversation
			`You spend a little while stretching your legs here on the <origin> spaceport, watching the various ships come in and go out and looking over the wide variety of Successors that mill about them. In many ways it's not unlike human space, though the elegance and efficiency with which the Successors build and operate their spaceports gives some hint about the much greater experience they have as an interstellar species.`
			`	Some things are just the same, though, like the news display that you realize is right above you as it lets out a particularly noticeable warble. It catches your eye for a moment; the program is presenting a visualization of what the attack on House Seineq's base could have plausibly looked like, a well of morphic metal unspooling from the display to form small simulated Vujleten flying in formation, firing their weapons, and even cloaking themselves once they've delivered their payloads, their forms growing indistinct and wavy as the liquid metal returns to its origin.`
			`	As the narrator intones something about historical uses of cloaking technology, a spark of understanding suddenly lights in your mind: you recall your last conversation with Saajret and their story about the camouflaging Kijran-Khora, and in light of House Kaatrij's blockade over <planet>, how they might have been offering you a way that you could investigate Kaatrij's base for yourself. The moon's atmosphere is thin enough that a cloaked ship could probably approach the surface totally undetected, even considering the no-doubt advanced scanners House Kaatrij is using to detect intruders.`
				accept



mission "Successors: Ghosts 8"
	priority
	landing
	source "Qasa-Sija-Iri"
	to offer
		or
			has "Successors: Ghosts 7a: done"
			has "Successors: Ghosts 7b: done"
	on offer
		conversation
			`As you enter orbit over <origin>, you can see that House Kaatrij continues to occupy the planet's surface, scanning and intercepting any ships that might attempt to land.`
			choice
				`	(Cloak.)`
					to activate
						has "flagship attribute: cloak"
					goto cloaked
				`	(Continue down.)`
				`	(Leave.)`
					depart
			`	The <ship> is soon detected by Kaatrij's scanners, and you are forced to return to orbit lest you face destruction.`
				depart
			label cloaked
			action
				set "successors: ghosts seen quarg"
			`	The hull of the <ship> warbles as its cloaking equipment engages, and as the seconds pass it becomes clear that Kaatrij's ships cannot detect you above the mostly-airless moon. Though you must descend slowly to avoid disturbing the atmosphere, you eventually find your way over the sandy surface to right above the now-revealed base House Kaatrij went to so much effort to hide.`
			`	As you once saw in the news broadcast, the outline of it is an enormous circle several kilometers in radius. Though the shimmering effect is now gone and some of the damage has been repaired, much of it still remains visible and there appears to be ongoing work on the damaged sections - House Kaatrij-registered freighters land on temporary landing pads and offload massive amounts of materials, some familiar, some not.`
			`	Most striking of all, however, is the appearance of some familiar-looking dark metal and purple lighting in the damaged section of the base; it's hard to be certain, but it bears a distinct resemblance to Quarg technology. Perhaps the Quarg might be able to provide some answers about what's been going on.`
			`	Not long after you see this, a thin sandstorm starts to roll in, and you take the <ship> back up to orbit before the mysterious absence of airborne grit gives your ship away.`
				flee

	on decline
		log "Approached the base on Qasa-Sija-Iri while under cloak. Its design vaguely resembles Quarg construction - perhaps they have some answers about what's been going on with the Successors."



mission "Successors: Ghosts 9"
	landing
	source
		attributes "human quarg" "hai quarg"
	to offer
		has "successors: ghosts seen quarg"
	on offer
		conversation
			`Do you want to ask the Quarg here about their base on the Successor moon Qasa-Sija-Iri?`
			choice
				`	(Yes.)`
				`	(Not now.)`
					defer
			`	Though so far individual Quarg have seemed equivalent in their ability to answer your questions, it is several minutes before you spot one here who, for some reason, seems like it would be able to answer. When you repeat your question to it, it blinks slowly, and answers even more so.`
			`	"I see," it says. "You have uncovered one of our great secrets of the galaxy. You were right to think that the world you speak of is ours. After what that foolish species did to themselves, we the Quarg could not bear to leave them unobserved. But we dared not do so unshrouded, lest we once again rouse them to the heights of envy - so we built no ringworld, no stations, no open worlds. Only a little... watching post, to keep our gaze over the Myiara."`
			`	You interject. "The Myiara? Do you mean the Successors?"`
			`	The Quarg considers the term. "Before they called themselves that, they were the Myiara. Have they truly become so rooted in their memories of their valorous past?" It makes a noise like the rumbling of distant thunder. "You must have questions."`
			choice
				`	"What is it that they did to themselves? Did they build some kind of terrible weapons?"`
					goto what
				`	"I didn't think hiding away was in your nature."`
					goto hiding

			label what
			`	"No," says the Quarg, "not weapons. That you have met them shows that you have found, or stolen, the secret to sail between the stars unhindered. Long, long ago, the Drak discovered that secret for the first time, and after many years, they shared it with us, the Quarg, so that peace and amity might reign in the galaxy. Then, only a few thousand human years ago, the Myiara found it too." The Quarg blinks slowly, and its whole body slumps as if burdened by a great sorrow.`
			`	"What they discovered was not what the Drak had, nor the beauty that the Korath, despite all their warring, had wrought. It was a new and dangerous thing, and while it let them explore with new freedom, in the years that followed, its mark became clear. It rent wounds among the stars, tore apart the paths between them, led their ships away to nowhere, and turned their verdant worlds to ash."`
			choice
				`	"Why did you allow them to develop something so destructive?"`
					goto allow
				`	"How did you keep yourselves hidden for so long?"`
					goto hiding

			label allow
			`	"They were then upon the precipice of a great change. Their long-wrought divisions were melding; they had turned away from the gruesome vagaries of war, and were moved to explore and preserve the arts of others. We hoped," and the Quarg imparts a heightened tone on this word, "that in time, they could become as we are, guardians and friends to all. Our judgment was clouded by our desire for this."`
			choice
				`	"It's hard to believe they were ever so unified."`
				`	"You saw them as equals to yourselves?"`
			`	A demeanor of great reflection passes over the Quarg, and then is gone just as quickly. "The Myiara were like... children, just beginning to conceive of and adopt the responsibilities that lie beyond youth. Full of cleverness and arrogance still, but borne aloft by a new-blooming capacity to see beyond themselves and their own base concerns."`
			choice
				`	"How did you keep yourself hidden from them for so long?"`

			label hiding
			`	"Hiding indeed does not come naturally to us," the Quarg says. "With no other have we had need to conceal ourselves. One of their Houses, when it knew what they had done, agreed to work with us to preserve their species. They were most skilled in matters of illusion, and shared their cloaks with us to obscure our presence."`
				goto end

			label end
			`	"What troubles this one most, though," says the Quarg, "is that this watching post of ours was laid bare to see at all. We made ourselves rancid to the Myiara for their own good, stole away their precious creations, worked with those of them who would help us to tear down so much of what they had built, sealed them away - all so they would not have the means to recreate their folly in a later age. That this deception of ours has come to light may drive them even further from what they were, undo even the meager gains they have wrought in their exile. For all their wrong, that would still be a cause for lament."`
			`	With that, the Quarg offers you a gentle bow. "Goodbye now, Captain," they say, and quietly walk away.`
				decline

	on decline
		set "successors: myiara name"
		log "Spoke with the Quarg, who revealed that they have kept a base on Qasa-Sija-Iri to monitor the Successors. It has remained cloaked by House Kaatrij, who has collaborated with the Quarg since the collapse of the Predecessors."
		log "Factions" "Successors" "The Successor species is properly referred to as the Myiara, though this term has fallen out of favor since the collapse of their old empire."



mission "Successors: Ghosts 10"
	landing
	name "Meet with House Kaatrij"
	description "Having allied with House Kaatrij, go with one of their military ships to their base at <destination>."
	source
