		has "successors: ghosts dealt with aqrabe"
	on offer
		conversation
			`As disembark from your ship, you notice a group of Successor soldiers emerging from another craft in the spaceport, a Seiitej bearing House Kaatrij's colors. They meet you outside your own vessel, their weapons held at attention.`
			`	"Captain <first> <last>," their leader says, "We've been instructed to take thee with us."`
			choice
				`	"For what purpose exactly?"`
					goto purpose
				`	"And if I refuse?"`
			`	"That would not be wise," the officer says. "Thou shalt understand, we trust?"`
				goto interrogation

			label purpose
			`	"Kaatrij wishes to speak with thee," says the lead officer. "And to hear what thou hast to say."`

			label interrogation
			`	With apparently no choice, you accompany the officers back to their ship; they remove your sidearm and take you to a room inside. Two stand guard over you while the rest attend to other things outside, and it's only after the better part of an hour that someone else finally enters, a tall Successor who looks over you with an incisive glare.`
			`	"Captain <first> <last>," they say. "How didst thou acquire cloaking technology?"`
			choice
				`	"It comes from another society, far away from here."`
				`	"I was given it by a human government; they found it in an alien cargo hold."`
					to display
						has "outfit (all): Cloaking Device"
			`	"So it was not given to thee by a faction here, among the Successors?"`
			`	"No," you say. The Successor relaxes, if only a little. "We will search thy ship t'confirm this," they say. "But I do not believe thou liest."`
			branch "cloaks"
				has "flagship attribute: cloak"

			choice
				`	"You won't find anything, my current ship isn't cloak-capable."`
			`	The Successor looks over you with a curious gaze. "Intriguing," they say. "'Tis no matter; we shall consult our records of thy craft."`

			label cloaks
			`	After a moment passes, your interrogator leans over you and the guards in the back stand, attentive. "Now we must decide what is to be done with thee," they say, "now that thou hast learned of our arrangement with the Quarg. Thou shouldst understand we do not wish that information to be avail'ble to all. Not all the Houses nor their members regard the Quarg with amity."`
			choice
				`	"I have no intention of spilling your secret."`
					goto discreet
				`	"I'll keep my lips sealed, for a price."`
					goto blackmail
				`	"The people deserve to know about this."`

			`	"Perhaps they shall one day, but neither thee nor I should decide that now. 'Tis a time far too fraught to bring such a thing to light. No," they say, one of their arms moving toward you, "but Kaatrij would be willing to offer thee an alternative: a formal relation with the House, that thou mightst be brought into our circle of knowledge and receive our boons. And, of course, be subject to our directives, including those of silence."`
			choice
				`	"And what would House Sioeora think of this?"`
					to display
						has "successors sioeora patron"
					goto sioeora
				`	"What would that entail, exactly?"`
					goto details
				`	"Yes, if it finally gets me some answers."`
					goto yes
				`	"No, I'm not willing to lie for you."`
					goto no

			label blackmail
			`	"Thou shouldst be careful with such propositions, Captain," they say. Their skin remains a murky, ashen blue. "Kaatrij would be willing to offer thee an alternative, however: a formal relation with the House, that thou mightst be brought into our circle of knowledge and receive our boons. Of course, thou wouldst also be subject to our directives, including those of silence. Wouldst that be sufficient reward for thine efforts?"`
			choice
				`	"And what would House Sioeora think of this?"`
					to display
						has "successors sioeora patron"
					goto sioeora
				`	"And what would that entail, exactly?"`
					goto details
				`	"Yes, if it finally gets me some answers."`
					goto yes
				`	"No, I think I'll stick to credits."`
					goto no

			label discreet
			action
				set "Successors: Ghosts: discreet"
			`	"Most discreet, Captain," they say. "But forgive me for not taking thy word alone. To that, Kaatrij is willing to make thee an offer: a formal relation with our House, that thou mightst be brought into our circle of knowledge and receive our boons. And in turn, thou wouldst also be subject to our directives, including those of silence. An arrangement, Kaatrij believes, of mutual benefit."`
			choice
				`	"And what would House Sioeora think of this?"`
					to display
						has "successors sioeora patron"
					goto sioeora
				`	"And what would that entail, exactly?"`
					goto details
				`	"Yes, if it finally gets me some answers."`
					goto yes
				`	"No, I prefer to remain a free agent."`
					goto no

			label sioeora
			`	Incendiary yellow speckles dot the Successor's face, and they continue with some small hint of satisfaction. "No doubt they would be displeas'd to have lost one they so dearly wish'd to possess. But they have fail'd to act with swiftness. What sayest thou to our offer?"`
			choice
				`	"All right, I'll do it."`
					goto yes
				`	"No, I don't want to get any more tangled up in this than I already am."`
					goto no

			label details
			`	"Thou wouldst be counted as an alien vassal of House Kaatrij, thus granted access to our facilities, subject to our rules and directives, and empowered to fight our enemies on our behalf under a commission of war. Thou wouldst retain thy freedom of movement, thine ability to go elsewhere in the galaxy. But when thou dost travel 'tween the stars of the Successors, 'tis House Kaatrij that thou shalt call thy home."`
			choice
				`	"All right, I accept."`
					goto yes
				`	"No, I don't want to get any more tangled up in this than I already am."`
					goto no

			label yes
			action
				set "successors kaatrij vassal"
				event "successors: ghosts unrestrict"
				"reputation: House Kaatrij" >?= 2
			`	"Excellent," the Successor says. "I would have thee come with us, then, to the moon where this all began, our base on <planet>. There, some of thy no-doubt-pressing questions shall be answered."`
				accept

			label no
