	npc save
		government `House Kaatrij`
		personality launching heroic escort
		ship "Seiitej" "Diri, Defiant Nnesa"

	on complete
		log "Formally inducted as a vassal of House Kaatrij, with all the attendant responsibilities and rewards."
		log "People" "Kampa" "One of House Kaatrij's fleet captains and a leader in their effort to unmask and retaliate against the attacker that damaged their base on Qasa-Sija-Iri."
		conversation
			`You once again descend to the dusty moon, though this time with the authorization to pass through the blockade. The ring-shaped base is now nowhere to be seen, but as you proceed to your landing coordinates, a shimmering aperture opens in the sand to reveal an advanced landing bay. As you set the <ship> down inside it, the top closes up again, sealing you off from the outside. Your hear the deep hum of motors and a faint sense of weightlessness as the whole landing bay plunges deep into the moon's crust, and only once it comes to a stop do the ground crew permit you to exit with an escort of House Kaatrij soldiers.`
			`	The inside of the facility is unlike that of any other Successor spaceport; though most of the structure features Successor - or to the Quarg, Myiaran - technology, the visual style of the interior shows a distinct Quarg influence. Though most of those who walk the spacious halls are Successors, every so often you catch a glimpse of a Quarg loping its way down a corridor or across an open area.`
			`	Your escort finally stops outside a gleaming white door, indicating for you to open it.`
			choice
				`	(Go inside.)`
					goto inside
				`	"What should I expect?"`
			`	The leader of the soldiers escorting you says nothing, instead only gesturing toward the door with a little more force. Getting the hint, you enter.`

			label inside
			`	Three figures stand on the other side: one is the Successor who interrogated you, one you recognize as Saajret, and the third is a Quarg who stands overlooking the other two. All three focus their eyes on you as the door opens, the Successors splaying their arms in polite greeting, the Quarg merely examining you.`
			`	"Captain <last>, 'tis good of thee to join us," the first Successor says. "We have not had a formal introduction, I recall. My name is Kampa; I lead one of Kaatrij's fleets. Thou hast already made acquaintance with Saajret, of Somber Sejra, of course." Saajret bows gently at this, their skin warbling with faint colors. "Already thine induction to our circles presents us with tasks for thee, but there is aught we must complete before that: to formalize the process."`
			`	They produce a data-sphere which they give over to you. It feels slightly cold to the touch. "Thine acceptance binds thee to this House as vassal; herefore it shall expect of thee thine support and secrecy, and thou might expect from it the powers and privileges thou might require. Dost thou accept?"`
			choice
				`	"I do."`
					goto yes
				`	"Maybe this was a bad idea."`
					goto uncertain
				`	"Does this mean you'll sell me weapons and warships?"`

			`	A color flits upon Kampa's face, but you can't quite tell if it's amusement or suspicion. "Strictly, yes, but such exchanges are governed by treaty. For the moment, while thine alignment with us is still unclear to the rest, Kaatrij declines this responsibility."`
			choice
				`	"All right, I formally accept."`
					goto yes
				`	"Maybe this was a bad idea."`

			label uncertain
			`	"Thou hast already seen this place, Captain, hast already accepted in word if not in bond. Thou art... too far in already."`
			choice
				`	"I suppose I am."`

			label yes
			`	The data-sphere flares with color, registering your assent. "'Tis done then," Kampa says. "Welcome to House Kaatrij." Both Kampa and Saajret bow again, the Quarg the only one in the room remaining motionless. "Thou shalt have access to much of our works, which now thou mightst explore at thy leisure. When thou'rt ready, thou shouldst meet Saajret at the spaceport here for thy first official task for us."`
			choice
				`	"You said you would answer my questions."`
				`	(Stay silent.)`
					goto end

			`	"Very well," Kampa says. "Thou may'st query as thou please."`
			label questions
			choice
				`	"That's all."`
					to display
						has "Successors: attack"
						has "Successors: drone"
						has "Successors: seineq"
						has "Successors: cloak"
						has "Successors: quarg"
					goto end
				`	"Do you know who attacked your base?"`
					to display
						not "Successors: attack"
					goto attack
				`	"Are you behind the drone ships in Predecessor space?"`
					to display
						not "Successors: drone"
					goto drone
				`	"What exactly is this arrangement with the Quarg that you have?"`
					to display
						not "Successors: quarg"
					goto quarg
				`	"How much cloaking technology do you actually have?"`
					to display
						not "Successors: cloak"
						has "Successors: attack"
					goto cloak
				`	"Did you attack House Seineq?"`
					to display
						has "Successors: attack"
						has "Successors: drone"
						has "Successors: cloak"
						not "Successors: seineq"
					goto seineq

			label attack
			action
				set "Successors: attack"
			`	"'Twas one of the High Houses, but which exactly, we do not know yet for certain." Kampa contemplates for a moment. "Each of the Houses keeps a few heirloom warships from the time of the old empire, and most dare not bring them from the gilded vaults where they lie, for they are far too precious to risk in petty conflicts. Yet another still fielded one of theirs, raided the moon, killed hundreds, all to steal a single cloaking unit. Now they flit about unseen."`
				goto questions

			label seineq
			action
				set "Successors: seineq"
			`	There's a pause as Kampa looks at you with incisive eyes. "Thou'rt fair to ask it," they say. "No," they say, "'twas not Kaatrij that struck them. Once our cloak was stolen, our 'lusive foe had all 'twas needed t'frame us of that trait'rous blow: t'let themselves be seen with signs that we alone had once posses'd."`
				goto questions

			label drone
			action
				set "Successors: drone"
			`	Kampa's skin ripples with hollow mirth. "Not exactly," they say. "'Twere creations of an ally of the old House Kaatrij during the last great inter-Houses war, a bold engineer of Aqrabe. Autonomous as they were, they could - when stripp'd of those drives that spoiled the savor of our victory - remain to ward off plund'rers of our cities and hidden vaults."`
				goto questions

			label cloak
			action
				set "Successors: cloak"
			`	"I shan't tell thee exactly," Kampa says. "Thy retrieval of the stellar metal for Aqrabe has been a boon to us in that, though."`
				goto questions
			
			label quarg
			action
				set "Successors: quarg"
			`	"We do not claim to be the equals of the Quarg in wisdom or grace," says Kampa, "but we share an affection for our species, and we would not see ourselves destroyed. The Quarg benefit from our cloaks and these dusty lands of ours; in turn, we have their counsel and consideration and, as 'tis necessary, some small material support."`
				goto questions

			label next
			action
				clear "Successors: attack"
				clear "Successors: drone"
				clear "Successors: seineq"
				clear "Successors: cloak"
				clear "Successors: quarg"

			label end
			`	With that said, Kampa leaves the room, as does a distracted-looking Saajret soon after. As you also turn to go and explore the facility, the Quarg, still watching, stops you as it starts to speak. "Do you believe that the threads of the universe must tend to constrict?" it says in your own language. "Perhaps there is something inherent in separation that existence abhors." It hums, a deep and organic rumble. "You may go. Saajret waits for you in the spaceport."`

	on fail
		dialog phrase "successor ghosts story failed"



mission "Successors: Ghosts 11"
	name "Visit Kaatrij archive"
	description "Take Saajret to <planet stopovers> so they can consult one of House Kaatrij's offworld archives, before returning them to <planet>."
	source "Qasa-Sija-Iri"
	stopover "Kasi-Osolaa-Sossa"
	passengers 1
	to offer
		has "Successors: Ghosts 10: done"
	on offer
		conversation
			`Saajret meets you in a room overlooking your ship, once again dressed in their black pocket-laden outfit. They bow as you approach.`
			choice
				`	"What's our task?"`
					goto task
				`	"How have you been?"`
			branch helped
				has "Successors: Ghosts 7a: done"

			`	Saajret hums, colors of preoccupation dancing over their skin. "Well enough to focus on what's before us," they say. They pull their body into a more rigid posture.`
				goto task

			label helped
			`	Saajret hums, colors of preoccupation dancing over their skin. "Well enough to focus on what's before us," they say. "I shall thank thee again for indulging my little trip into the past. The sense of it stays with me." They shake their head and offer you another gentle bow.`

			label task
			`	"Kaatrij maintains a number of offworld archives for our files since the time of our Predecessors. I've a certain angle I'd like to investigate at our archive on <planet stopovers>. Would'st thou transport me?"`
			choice
				`	"What sort of angle?"`
				`	"I can't right now."`
					defer

			`	Saajret nods. "Kampa believes 'twas an heirloom warship of the Houses that was used against us. By comparing our scan data of the attack with historical information of ships used before our Predecessors' exile, I think I may be able to determine exactly which ship it was that struck us. And with it, the House that lies behind it."`
			choice
				`	"All right, let's go."`
					accept
				`	"I can't right now."`
					defer

	on stopover
		"Successors: Ghosts Saajret Forgiveness" ++
		conversation
			`Saajret directs you to land at a small facility set into the ground in the midst of one of this planet's forests. A couple of guards greet the two of you at the entrance, where Saajret presents their authorization, inserting a small data-chip into a pad beside the facility's door while a scanner beam passes over them. They wave you inside once the process is complete.`
			`	The archive proves to be relatively modest by Successor standards; most of the engineering effort seems to have gone into armor rather than lush adornment. The two of you walk between long rows of storage units, each one suspending thousands of individual data-spheres in a bath of liquid metal. Saajret stops at a corner terminal in a section labeled for records between the years 1620 and 1636 and, after a few minutes of work, several data-spheres are bubbled up from one of the surrounding storage baths.`
			`	Saajret plugs the spheres into the terminal and you watch over their shoulder as they consult the data within; what appears to be a mixture of dossiers on warships of the era and biographical data about their engineers. Saajret's skin blotches with confusion.`
			choice
				`	"What is it?"`
				`	"Have you found what you're looking for?"`
			`	Saajret hums. "To our knowledge," they say, "twenty-three heirloom warships were smuggled through the wormhole in our Predecessors' era. Of these, six were fast battlecruisers, named Valkkyiaran - and of those, only three could possibly be the craft that struck at Qasa-Sija-Iri. Their names were Alasii-i-Lua, Ijahti-Khora, and Akhos-Itran."`
			choice
				`	"Do you know what House they belonged to?"`
				`	"Is there no way to tell which one exactly was behind the attack?"`
			`	"That is where misfortune meets us," Saajret says. "All three of those were made for a combined alliance that fought in the last great inter-Houses war; when t'were disassembled and smuggled away, we know not which House of the alliance spirited each away. Much remains unclear."`
			choice
				`	"Do you have any data on the drone ships?"`
				`	"We'd better return, then."`
					goto end

			`	"A good thought, captain," Saajret says. A difficult-to-identify emotion flits over their skin as they return to the terminal. They download some of the biographical data they were consulting into a portable data-sphere and, once they have tracked down data pertaining to the ships themselves, download that as well.`
			`	The drone ships themselves were designed by a Myiara named Resja, a noted shipwright for the old House Aqrabe. Initially, the craft were designed for small crews, but after Resja's death - apparently by poisoning - they were retrofitted with drone cores and robotic maintenance systems, after which they served first as expendable rearguards and finally as the lingering defense systems that you've encountered.`
			`	The biographical data is added to your log.`

			action
				"Successors: Ghosts Saajret Forgiveness" -= 2
				set "successors: ghosts resja biography"
				log "People" "Resja" "Resja was a noted Myiaran engineer and shipwright who worked soon before the collapse of the empire of the Myiaran Predecessors, circa 1600. They are responsible for designing the originally-crewed drone ships that linger in Predecessor space, later retrofitted as self-guided craft after Resja's death by poisoning."

			label end
			`	With Saajret satisfied that the two of you have gleaned what information you can, you both return to the <ship> outside.`

	on complete
		dialog "Saajret thanks you for transporting them and asks to meet you back in one of the spaceport planning rooms once they have shown their data to Kaatrij's military officers."

	on fail
		dialog phrase "successor ghosts story failed"



