mission "Successors: Ghosts 13"
	landing
	name "Deliver keystone shipment"
	description "Return the <tons> of <cargo> to <destination>."
	source "Kasii-Cavasaa-Oa"
	destination "Qasa-Sija-Iri"
	cargo "Harmonic Keystones" 16
	to offer
		has "Successors: Ghosts 12: done"
	on offer
		conversation
			branch "prototypes only"
				not "event: successors: ghosts keystones finished"

			`Not long after disembarking you are met by Tiliia, the Aqrabe engineer you worked with before. They splay their arms courteously to you while, behind them, crates of keystones are carried by and soon loaded into the <ship>.`
			`	"I thought it fair to see this shipment off myself," Tiliia says by way of introduction. "Though it pleaseth me to see thee again as well, Captain."`
			choice
				`	"Likewise."`
					goto short
				`	"I'm surprised you're letting go of the keystones so easily."`

			`	Some mirth seems to come over Tiliia. "We've enough to do so now. And I imagine House Kaatrij has offered Aqrabe generous compensation for them, too. It's good they're trading with us at all now. If only I could work fast enough to satisfy that appetite for novelty!"`

			label short

			`	The two of you chat for a few more minutes as the keystones are loaded. Eventually, Tiliia offers you a "farewell" before returning to their work and leaving you to prepare your ship for departure.`
				accept

			label "prototypes only"
			`Not long after disembarking you are met by Tiliia, the Aqrabe engineer you worked with recently. They offer you a perfunctory and hurried splay of the arms. "Thou'rt here for the keystone shipment, I take it?" they say in a clipped tone. You nod in reply. "Well, Kaatrij will get their sixteen tons, but let them know they're only prototypes. Politics moves faster than my work." They turn to depart, clearly eager to get back to it, before stopping and offering you a quick "good to see thee, Captain," before they leave you to oversee the loading of the keystones.`
				accept

