mission "Successors: Ghosts 14"
	name "Destroy sensor probes"
	description "House Kaatrij is concerned that the sensor probes in Predecessor space are being used against them, and have asked you to destroy them in <waypoints>."
	passengers 1
	source "Qasa-Sija-Iri"
	waypoint "Khasola-Ryuit"
	waypoint "Eta Carinae"
	waypoint "Avasaa-Novaa"
	to offer
		has "Successors: Ghosts 13: done"
	on offer
		conversation
			`Saajret meets you in another one of the spaceport's overlooking rooms, a liquid-metal starchart laid out on a table before them. It looks like it's showing areas of Predecessor space. They greet you with a splay of the arms as you enter.`
			`	"Is this my next mission?" you ask, gesturing to the starchart.`
			`	Saajret hums thoughtfully. "Yes," they say. "One of the things thou did earli'r was the placement of scanning eyes throughout the Shroud, at Seineq's dear request."`
			choice
				`	"I recall."`
					goto direct
				`	"Could Seineq be the House behind the attack?"`

			`	Whorls of pink mirth erupt over Saajret's skin. "Perhaps so, perhaps not," they say. "For now, Kaatrij's aim is more direct. The eyes make notes of jumps of the proper sort, as are made by thine own craft and the Quarg - but the flitting of our foe relies on aught uncanni'r that we believe evades their gaze. Thus, as Kampa's wont to say, they are to us a tactical disadvantage. Kaatrij seeks that thou, and I, observing, destroy them."`
				goto questions

			label direct
			`	"Kaatrij now seeks that thou undoeth this, with my presence as observer. 'Thout Seineq's control of those, our foe might come to watch them - 'tis a risk Kaatrij is loath to take. For they make note of jumps of the proper sort, as made by thy craft and the Quarg's alike. But the flitting of our foe relies on aught uncanni'r that we think evades their gaze. Thus, they reveal not the comings and goings of the guilty but thee and perhaps our own craft."`

			label questions
			choice
				`	"Why are you joining me?"`
					to display
						not "Successors: you"
					goto you
				`	"What do you mean, 'something uncannier?'"`
					to display
						not "Successors: uncannier"
					goto uncannier
				`	"All right, I'm ready to go."`
					accept

			label uncannier
			action
				set "Successors: uncannier"
			`	Saajret's skin bubbles with dark blue spots. "The Quarg say thou hast already learn'd of our Predecessors' efforts to sail beyond the bound'ries set by the Drak. The drives 'twere built to do this are that uncanny thing of which I speak."`
				goto questions

			label you
			action
				set "Successors: you"
			`	Saajret hums. "Thy presence here is still new, captain, and Kaatrij would not send thee far 'thout someone to look over thee. And for myself particularly," they say, looking out at your ship below them, "I have spoken to thee the most, and my role as archivist makes me knowledgeable of the things we may find in the blighted worlds of the Shroud."`
				goto questions

	on enter "Khasola-Ryuit"
		dialog `Though it takes several seconds for your ship's targeting scanners to pinpoint the scanning probe you deployed earlier, they eventually find it. A single shot is all it takes to destroy it.`

	on enter "Eta Carinae"
		dialog `You find the scanner tucked among some particularly vibrant nebular gas. It is easily dispatched.`

	on enter "Avasaa-Novaa"
		dialog `Undoing your earlier hard work, you locate and destroy the scanner in this system.`

	on waypoint
		dialog `With this system cleared, you've destroyed all the sensor probes except the one in Kasii-Sola.`
		event "successors: ghosts ijra-ea decloak"
		clear "Successors: you"
		clear "Successors: uncannier"

	on fail
		dialog phrase "successor ghosts story failed"



mission "Successors: Ghosts 15"
	passengers 1
	transition
	name "Destroy final sensor probe"
	description "Having destroyed the other sensor probes, go to <waypoints> to destroy the fourth and final one before returning to <destination>."
	waypoint "Kasii-Sola"
	destination "Qasa-Sija-Iri"
	to offer
		has "event: successors: ghosts ijra-ea decloak"
	on enter "Kasii-Sola"
		conversation
			`As you enter the system, your ship's sensors remark on an object that wasn't here the last time: a space station has appeared in close solar orbit. Every few seconds your lock on the station breaks before it is quickly reacquired.`
			`	Saajret's look at examining the station is one of despair. "Wretches!" they say. "We shall need to address this upon returning. Our time is running short, Captain. Let us destroy the fourth probe with haste."`
			choice
				`	"You recognize that station?"`
				`	"What's going on here?"`
			`	Saajret hums for a moment. "Fine, fine. It's one of ours, a citadel of old Kaatrij from bygone years. 'Twas cloaked, of course. 'Til now, t'would seem; and so we are outmaneuvered again. That is why we must be quick, Captain; thou mustn't delay."`
				accept

	on complete
		conversation
			`While you are presenting your landing authorization, Saajret calls for several members of Kaatrij to meet you in the docking bay; by the time you land, they are there waiting, slithering over to speak to Saajret almost immediately. The leader of this group dismisses you and Saajret, with an apologetic bow, asks you to meet them at the <planet> spaceport in an hour.`

	on fail
		dialog phrase "successor ghosts story failed"



mission "Successors: Saajret Remarks"
	entering
	invisible
	source
		not attributes "tangled shroud" "predecessor" "successor"
	destination "Earth"
	to offer
		or
			has "Successors: Ghosts 14: active"
			has "Successors: Ghosts 15: active"
	on offer
		"Successors: Ghosts Saajret Openness" ++ # Increases as Saajret experiences new, interesting, and joyful things.
		conversation
			`As the stygian fog of the Tangled Shroud fades away to reveal normal space, Saajret makes a small noise of excitement, their skin dancing with bright hues. "So long it's been," they say, "since one of ours has seen beyond the horizon of our folly. I confess I wonder what the rest of the galaxy has become after fifteen hundred years of solitude." They shake their head, the regions of color splashing like water. "Yet our task remains. Perhaps in some future time..."`
			choice
				`	"There are more things in heaven and earth, Saajret, than are dreamed of in your philosophy."`
				`	"The galaxy isn't all you make it out to be, at least in my experience."`
			`	They hum, long and slow. "Perhaps," they say.`
				decline



mission "Successors: Ghosts 16"
	name "Investigate mysterious station"
	description "Return to the mysterious station in <system> with Saajret to investigate what has happened to it."
	source "Qasa-Sija-Iri"
	destination "Ijra-Ea, Shimmering Veil"
	to offer
		has "Successors: Ghosts 15: done"
	npc save
		government `House Kaatrij`
		personality launching heroic escort
		ship "Vujlet-Usaqri (Jump)" "o-Sapi, Brilliant Voice"
	on offer
		conversation
			`Saajret meets with you in a small room about fifteen degrees around the ring of the cloaked facility. It's circular with a shallow pool in the middle; something similar to moss crawls up the walls and a couple of small flowering plants poke their colorful heads up underfoot.`
			`	"My thanks to thee for thy help so far," Saajret says. "I hope thou hast found our little shared space here comfortable enough."`
			choice
				`	"I have."`
				`	"What's the situation with that station?"`
			`	Saajret nods. "I've conferred with Kaatrij and our Quarg patrons and, for once, we are all agreed. Two tasks lie before us, with thou included if thou wilt: first, we must assess how our citadel has been plunder'd. 'Tis well-defended, and seeing as its cloak was not fully disabled, its security must remain at least partially op'rative. For this, thou might'st play a vital role, again with thy unhind'red craft."`
			label "questions 1"
			choice
				`	"'Security?' Not sure I like the sound of that."`
					to display
						not "Successors: security"
					goto security
				`	"How could it have been revealed in the first place?"`
					to display
						not "Successors: revealed"
					goto revealed
				`	"What's the second task?"`
					goto second

			label security
			action
				set "Successors: security"
			`	Saajret prods a flower on the floor with the tip of one of their arms. "I've been fashioned with keys to elude the station's own defenses. That which poses the most threat to us are the independent ones; thou hast before met the guardian drone ships? With the citadel reveal'd, no doubt one has already taken up residence there."`
				goto "questions 1"

			label revealed
			action
				set "Successors: revealed"
			`	"That may be the most pertinent question that faces us all now, Captain." Many-colored waves ripple over Saajret's skin. "The location of our citadel, I am now told, was known to precious few within Kaatrij and none without. It suggests what I've suspected all along; one within Kaatrij has betrayed the House, sold our secrets to another."`
				goto "questions 1"

			label second
			action
				clear "Successors: security"
				clear "Successors: revealed"
			`	"Secondly," says Saajret, "'tis clear we must end this flitting about in the shadow of our foe. While thou and I breach the citadel, Kaatrij and the Quarg here plan a trap to snare an heirloom warship. To destroy such a craft would be a great wound to our attacker, and would, if we are fortunate, give us some measure of their identity.`
			choice
				`	"How do you plan to catch it if it's cloaked?"`
				`	"All right, what's next?"`
					goto next
			`	The mess of colors dotting Saajret's face resolves into a unified shade of satisfaction. "The Quarg, it seems, have certain ways to uncover such hidden craft. An old foe of theirs used a similar tactic, I'm told. Convincing them to share aught is a lifetime task for the most persuasive of diplomats, but in this instance they may help us for the sake of quieting that ship's space-ripping drive. For that," they say, "they are most eager."`

			label next
			`	A fine mist is emitted by ports on the ceiling, watering the plants and gathering in tiny spheres on your clothes. "We should prepare for our journey to the citadel. Equip thy craft as thou desireth, then let us depart."`
				accept

	on complete
		conversation
			`As you approach a central docking port on the citadel, alarms momentarily ring throughout the <ship>'s bridge as numerous weapon locks are detected. A moment later they cease and Saajret radios you from their own craft that it is safe to land, the shape of the Vujlet disappearing into the station's wide mouth.`
			`	The inside is truly cavernous; the circular vault of the station's core forms an artificial sky, the landing pad for your ship a stamp-sized rectangle on its perimeter. Saajret exits from their landed ship and meets you with a pair of Kaatrij soldiers; you recognize one as having accompanied Kampa before when they interrogated you.`
			`	"I've added us as allies in the station's security rolls," says Saajret. "It should permit us access below." They check a data-pad that they produce from one of their pockets, looking from the shifting metallic screen to the layout of the docking bay. Eventually, they point to one of several circular apertures on the floor. As you approach, a large elevator pod emerges from it and its doors open expectantly.`
			choice
				`	"What's with the Myiara and these massive constructions?"`
				`	"How far down are we going?"`
					goto down
			`	Saajret is speckled with mirth and hums. "Myiara?" they say. "'Twas the Quarg that told thee this, no doubt. Ah, but to answer thy query: after the discovery of cloaks, Kaatrij's outposts grew smaller and more independent. This one was simply older, and 'twas no challenge in the day to clad even a citadel such as this in stellar metal. That way, even small generators could cloak it whole." They rub the tips of two of their arms over a data-sphere embedded in the elevator pod.`
			choice
				`	"How far down are we going?"`

			label down
			`	"We shall want to check the systems core and the vault, at least," says Saajret. "A very long way, for certain."`
			`	The elevator takes the four of you down for several minutes; every once in a while, a window to the outside shows individual flashes of the sun setting as the station continues in its orbit. It finally stops on a platform overlooking a vast, dizzyingly-tall space, where pillars rise up for what seems like kilometers below you and terminate kilometers above. Myriad cargo containers are attached to their sides, and between them rest eight gleaming starships. Some of the designs are familiar, like polished versions of those you've seen in Successor space; others are entirely new to you.`
			`	Saajret directs their two soldiers to set up a trio of small poles on the surface of the platform. They then radio to their ship and the poles light up, projecting barely-visible laser scanning beams throughout the vast space. After a couple of seconds, they mutter something to themself and order the soldiers to pack up the scanners.`
			choice
				`	"What is it?"`
				`	"Everything here that's supposed to be?"`
					goto everything
			`	"Kaatrij's fortune glows today," they say. "Naught lies out of place here; all is as 'twas when Kaatrij left it long ago."`
				goto core

			label everything
			`	"Fortunately," they say, "it is. Naught lies out of place; all is as 'twas when Kaatrij left it long ago."`
			label core
			`	You all return to the elevator and it once again begins to plunge you deeper into the citadel. You start to feel something prickling in your ear, but it is gone as soon as it began. The views of outside stop and the elevator shaft seems to grow darker and redder as the four of you travel deeper. Eventually it reaches another platform, but the door of the elevator refuses to open. Saajret enters some commands on the elevator controls, and the reason is revealed: as the elevator's door blushes transparent, you can see the corridor behind it has been perforated and torn open from outside. In the distance you can see a blast door leading into an armored, spherical construction, but that too has been blasted apart.`
			`	Saajret mutters darkly and once again orders the soldiers to set up the scanners, and once again they project their beams, now through the transparent door and into the breached segment. A wave of black ruffles over Saajret's skin. "All but one of the station's cloaking nodes have been remov'd. So strange..." they say, "to have stolen these and yet left the vault unassailed." The wave passes, leaving only colorlessness in its wake. "We must bring this news with haste. Let us hurry back."`
			`	All of a sudden, the station's comm system crackles to life. A rapid series of interweaving clicks emerge, and they soon shift and warp in your ears as your translation device begins to interpret them. "Interloper!" something screams, and you feel dizzy. "Despoiler! Invading wretch!"`
			choice
				`	(Rip off the translation device.)`
				`	(Try to block out the sounds.)`
			`	As soon as you move, something punches against your inner ear and you crumple to the ground. The screaming voice stops, and another one takes its place, less pointed but no less painful. "We recognize thy kind," it says. "And the other with thee, too. Saajret?" As their name is spoken, Saajret stands over you, their words unintelligible. The voice shifts again. "Deceiver!" it screams. "Thou who hast plundered beast and bone from where they shouldst forever lie!"`
			choice
				`	"I'm trying to stop the thieves!"`
				`	"How are you in my head!?"`
				`	"What about Saajret?"`
			`	The rage of the artificial voice chills. "Insignificant," it shouts, and as something else begins to interleave with the sound, something sharp and painful, there comes a quiet final phrase: "I missed thee," the voice says. "I missed thee."`
			`	And all of a sudden it stops; the pain, the voice. The pressure fades away from your head and Saajret looks down at you, the translation device plucked from your body and held in their arm. They help you to your feet and return it to you; you store it in a pocket, deactivated.`
			`	Saajret confers with their guards for a moment, their words a mess of unintelligible sound. One of them interacts with the elevator controls and the carriage starts to move upwards again, the station's com system shrieking to no avail. Saajret comes to speak to you, gently poking your chest with the tip of one of their arms; they say something that sounds a bit like your name. Suddenly the elevator is shaken by an impact from outside, and soon after dozens more follow. The four of you are deposited back in the landing bay just as you catch a glimpse of a ship in the distance firing on the station. You dash back to your own craft and prepare to flee or fight.`
				launch

	on fail
		dialog phrase "successor ghosts story failed"



