mission "Successors: Ghosts 18"
	landing
	name "Set up cloak detectors"
	description "Set up the Quarg cloak detectors on the far side of the Successors' wormhole before landing on <destination> to lay in wait for the heirloom warship."
	source "Qasa-Sija-Iri"
	destination "Myiara-Aret-Iir"
	cargo "Cloak detection node" 10
	to offer
		has "Successors: Ghosts 17: done"
	npc save
		government "House Kaatrij"
		personality launching heroic escort
		ship "Vujlet-Usaqri (Keystone)" "Tili, Open Arms"
		ship "Vujlet-Usaqri (Keystone)" "Jas, the Trees"
		ship "Vujlet-Usaqri (Keystone)" "Siij, of Able Ej"
		ship "Vujlet-Usaqri (Keystone)" "Luatet, Gentle Song"
		ship "Vujlet-Usaqri (Keystone)" "Ruu, of Votive Naaq"
	blocked "You need a ship with at least 10 units of free cargo space to begin this mission."
	on offer
		conversation
			branch deferred
				has "Successors: Ghosts 18: deferred"

			`Saajret meets you soon after you disembark, their voice once again being translated by your now-reactivated translation device. "I've no time to consult with thee immediately," they say, "but please join me once I've updated Kaatrij."`
			choice
				`	"Before you go! Thank you."`
				`	(Wait.)`
					goto briefing

			action
				"Successors: Ghosts Saajret Openness" ++
			`	The cool blue of satisfaction washes over Saajret's skin. "Thou art most welcome, Captain," they say, and leave you to wait.`

			label briefing
			`	While you wait, you notice the two scout ships that joined you in the Oublaa-Khora system have landed nearby. Three other Vujleten-Usaqri soon join them, forming a small fleet within one of the larger hangar bays of the spaceport.`
			`	After a while, one of the members of House Kaatrij comes to meet you and guides you to the same conference room you were shown on your first visit to the base. Inside stands Kampa, now dressed in an opulent uniform, along with Saajret and a number of Kaatrij's military officers.`
			`	"Captain <last>," Kampa says. "With Saajret's report on the Kasii-Sola citadel's plund'ring we've no time to squander." A metallic pool in the center of the room splashes and forms into a depiction of a warship, more sharp and elegant than any you've seen the Successors use.`
			`	"Another House," they say, "has dragg'd an heirloom starship from their reliquary and set it 'gainst us, and now used it t'steal no less than five sep'rable cloaks. So long as such a craft flies free, Kaatrij shan't know peace. To catch it, the Quarg provide us on loan some tools of theirs, detectors to wrap round the wormhole's mouth and catch our quarry when next it seeks to pass through.`
			`	Our plan's an ambush; a fleet of our own cloaked craft shall lay in wait for it and intercept it while 'tis stricken. The alien captain shall join them, should it please them."`
			label questions
			choice
				`	"My current ship isn't able to cloak."`
					to display
						not "flagship attribute: cloak"
					goto "no cloak"
				`	"What if the fleet is disabled?"`
					to display
						not "Successors: lose"
					goto lose
				`	"What sort of fight should I expect?"`
					to display
						not "Successors: expect"
					goto expect
				`	"All right, I'm ready."`
					to display
						has "flagship attribute: cloak"
					goto end
			label lose
			action
				set "Successors: lose"
			`	Kampa nods. "We've a second plan, with crews already prepar'd. But 'tisn't thy responsibility to know it."`
				goto questions

			label expect
			action
				set "Successors: expect"
			`	Saajret is the one who speaks now. "'Tis a proper battlecruiser of our Predecessors' age," they say. "Our warships in their day were second only to those of the Quarg; one could not doubt stand against a fleet of lesser craft handily."`
				goto questions

			label end
			`	Saajret speaks. "I'll join thee, <last>, before we depart. Thou shalt need a guide to the world where we seek to plan the ambush."`
				accept

			label "no cloak"
			action
				set "Successors: Ghosts 18: deferred"
			`	Kampa considers this for a moment. "The benefit of thy joining us outweighs the loss of a small delay," they say. "We can afford to wait on thee to acquire such a craft if it enables this ambush. Please act quickly if thou wish t'assist."`
				defer

			label deferred
			branch "still no cloak"
				not "flagship attribute: cloak"

			`	Having acquired a cloak-capable flagship, you are quickly directed back to a briefing room within the base where Kampa reiterates the plan: you will join a fleet of House Kaatrij's ships to deploy Quarg cloak detectors around the wormhole, before laying in wait on <destination> to ambush the heirloom warship that attacked Kaatrij.`
				accept

			label "still no cloak"
			`	Without a cloak-capable flagship, you cannot join House Kaatrij in their ambush.`
				defer


	on enter "Oublaa-Khora"
		dialog `As you exit the wormhole, you trigger the release of the cloak detector from your ship's cargo bay. The metal orb floats into position at the wormhole's edge before disappearing from view entirely as its cloaking armor activates. Apparently satisfied, Saajret directs you to land on the nearby planet.`

	on complete
		conversation
			`Once the rest of House Kaatrij's fleet has deployed their own cloak detectors, the fleet of Vujleten follow you into <planet>'s atmosphere, bedding down in the shadow of an ancient weather control tower to shield them from the dust. Several of the Successors inside exit to inspect the tower's functioning, and return after a few minutes. They bring long fuel hoses out of their ships and connect them to ports on the tower's side; one by one, the flock of Vujleten shimmer and then disappear as their own cloaks engage.`
			`	As one of the crew of the Kaatrij ships links the <ship>'s own fuel tank to the tower's reserves, Saajret slithers onto the bridge and greets you. "Now, it seems, we wait," they say. Black and white patterns of dots dance across their face, whirling around each other and occasionally splashing apart.`
			choice
				`	"What makes you think they'll even come back this way?"`
					goto retreat
				`	"How long will we be able to stay here?"`
			`	Saajret tilts their head to the side as the whirling colors slow. "Some few days, at most. The tower's fuel has mostly long since gone, and we drink now only the last dregs of it. I think we shall not need to, though," they say. "Soon after leaving, Kaatrij pulled its fleets from Aaura-Kaska, circled them around our core. 'Tis an invitation to the wormhole, we should think - fewer scans, fewer edits to one's course."`
				goto trap

			label retreat
			`	Saajret's skin sparkles with satisfaction. "Soon after leaving, Kaatrij pulled its fleets from Aaura-Kaska, circled them around our core. 'Tis an invitation to the wormhole, we should think - fewer scans, fewer edits to one's course. Open we leave the gate, and now something wicked this way comes."`

			label trap
			`	"Won't they think it could be a trap?"`
			`	"Perhaps." Outside, a gust of wind throws up enough grit to leave tiny blue flashes against the shields of one of the cloaked Vuljeten. "We've become our own quarries, though, isolated from our allies, no longer fearsome in scale. Surprise," they say, "is only worth so much."`
			`	Saajret excuses themself there, offering you a short bow and splay of the arms. With nothing left to do but wait, you and your crew work to prepare the <ship> for the forthcoming battle.`
			choice
				`	(Wait.)`
			`	In the early morning of the following day, an alarm rings on the bridge of the <ship>. Your sensors pick up the annihilation of countless antiprotons against the shields of a cloaked ship emerging from the wormhole and soon after, a new contact blinks into existence as its cloak fails. The radios between your ship and Kaatrij's spring to life as you all cut loose your fuel cables and take off.`
				launch

	on fail
		dialog phrase "successor ghosts story failed"



mission "Successors: Ghosts 19"
	landing
	name "Defeat the heirloom warship"
	description "Destroy the Myiaran heirloom warship with the help of House Kaatrij before returning to their base on <destination> for debriefing."
	source "Myiara-Aret-Iir"
	destination "Qasa-Sija-Iri"
	to offer
		has "Successors: Ghosts 18: done"
	npc kill
		government `High Houses (Unknown)`
		personality waiting heroic target unconstrained
		ship "Valkkyiara-Khorasaqra" "Ijahti-Khora"
		on kill
			set "Successors: Ghosts killed heirloom"
			dialog "With the warship destroyed, you should return to Qasa-Sija-Iri for debriefing."
	npc
		government "House Kaatrij"
		personality launching heroic escort
		ship "Vujlet-Usaqri (Keystone)" "Tili, Open Arms"
		ship "Vujlet-Usaqri (Keystone)" "Jas, the Trees"
		ship "Vujlet-Usaqri (Keystone)" "Siij, of Able Ej"
		ship "Vujlet-Usaqri (Keystone)" "Luatet, Gentle Song"
		ship "Vujlet-Usaqri (Keystone)" "Ruu, of Votive Naaq"
		on kill
			set "Successors: Ghosts support fleet died"
	on offer
		event "successors: ghosts abandoned kaatrij" 3
	on complete
		payment 10000000
		log "Fought and destroyed an heirloom warship of the High Houses with the support of House Kaatrij, likely the same ship that attacked their base on Qasa-Sija-Iri."
		conversation
			`As the <ship> returns to the Kaatrij base, it is scanned even more thoroughly than usual, planetary coilguns tracking it carefully until at last the scanners are satisfied. The portal in the sand opens to a curiously quiet scene; the whole facility seems to be waiting for whatever comes next. As soon as your landing gear touches ground, everything springs into motion.`
			`	Saajret slithers off almost immediately, only offering a hasty promise of their return and a poorly-concealed tint of satisfaction. You don't have to wait long, though; by the time the spaceport's automated repair arms have folded down to assess the <ship>'s battle damage, you notice Saajret coming back, Kampa and a smattering of Kaatrij officers at their side. Though none of the base's Quarg join them, you notice one watching the scene from one of the rooms overlooking the spaceport.`
			`	Kampa speaks first as they lead you away from your ship and into a more secluded region of the port. "'Tis good that thou prevail'd," they say, sharing in Saajret's satisfaction. "'Twas a fraught battle, I trust?"`
			choice
				`	"Indeed. We were lucky it was just one ship."`
					goto next
				`	"It was. I'm sorry none of your own crews survived."`
					to display
						has "Successors: Ghosts support fleet died"
					goto mournful
				`	"I've fought tougher."`

			`	"Indeed?" Kampa says. "Later thou shalt have to tell us more of this."`

			label mournful
			`	"As are we," says Kampa. "But their names shall be honored ones for their courage and devotion."`
			label next
			`	They produce a data-sphere from their outfit and offer it to you. As you take it, they continue, "I shall enjoy debriefing thee after our conversation here, but for now, Kaatrij has seen fit to offer thee a reward for thy able service. Since thou hast yet to receive the ability to purchase our technologies, today 'tis purely monetary. The sphere authorizes the transfer of <payment> to thee."`
			choice
				`	"Has this brought us any closer to knowing which House committed the attacks?"`
				`	"And what about purchasing your technology, since you mention it?"`
					goto technology
				`	"Thank you. It's most generous."`
					goto generous

			`	Kampa nods. "It shall, if fortune favors us. We've dispatched fleets to examine the wreckage left after the fray. There is little chance anything clearly identifying remains, but the wreckage may give valuable context to our intelligence."`
			`	Saajret interjects. "That wedding 'tween Myurej and Chydiyi, too, offers us an opportunity to observe the other Houses in the wake of this. One there has been wounded now, and we shall see if it shows."`
			`	"Such a gathering also fulfills the treaty conditions under which we may offer thee our license," says Kampa. "In short, we await it eagerly."`
				goto "what now"

			label technology
			`	Saajret nods here. "That wedding 'tween Myurej and Chydiyi is likely to happen soon," they say. "Thy time of shrouded service to Kaatrij has come to its close; with all the Houses there, 'tis a fair opportunity to present thee with our license."`
			`	"Thou hast done service to other Houses, too," Kampa says, "so it should be 'thout much resistance."`
				goto "what now"

			label generous
			`	Kampa bows and Saajret interjects. "That wedding 'tween Myurej and Chydiyi is likely to happen soon," they say. "And with it, the end to thy shrouded service to Kaatrij. 'Tis a fair time to present thee with our license, as much as it may interest thee."`
			`	"Thou hast done service to other Houses, too," Kampa says, "so it should be 'thout much resistance."`

			label "what now"
			choice
				`	"What now?"`
				`	"Do you have anything else for me?"`

			branch "wedding preparations"
				not "successors: ghosts dealt with myurej"

			`	"Just to wait," Kampa says. "Kaatrij must now determine its next move."`
				goto end

			label "wedding preparations"

			`	"On the matter of the forthcoming wedding," Kampa says. "Myurej continues to whine about some absent gifts of theirs. Shouldst thou need to earn thyself an invitation, that would be a matter to pursue."`

			label end

			`	With that said, Kampa bows and leaves. "I expect thou shouldst wish to supervise thy craft's repairs," Saajret says, "or perhaps merely enjoy some rest." Their skin speckles with mirth. "Farewell, Captain. I hope to see thee again soon."`

	on fail
		dialog phrase "successor ghosts story failed"



