# Intermission

mission "Successors: Ghosts 20"
	landing
	name "Go to the scions' wedding"
	description "The long-awaited wedding between scions of House Myurej and Chydiyi will take place at <destination> by <date>."
	source
		attributes "successor"
		not attributes "uninhabited"
	to offer
		random < 33
		has "Successors: Ghosts 19: done"
		has "successors: ghosts dealt with myurej"
	destination "Iyra-Ijasa-Iret"
	deadline 10
	on offer
		conversation
			`Shortly after landing here, a data-sphere is delivered to you. It jumps to life as soon as you touch it, displaying its message:`
			`	Honored alien who has earned audience at the gilded wedding 'tween Myurej and Chydiyi, we wish to inform thee that the date is set. Thy presence we shall cordially request at <planet> by <date>.`
			`	This is attested on behalf of Myurej M- Khiajsore, honored scion of House Myurej.`
				accept
	on complete
		log "Attended the wedding between scions of Houses Chydiyi and Myurej. Was presented with a license to purchase advanced Successor technology."
		set "license: High Houses"
		event "successors: ghosts intermission timer" 40
		event "successors: ghosts kaatrij expansion"
		conversation
			branch waterlining
				has "flagship attribute: waterlining"
			`You are given directions to one of the shallow-water landing pads on a secondary <planet> spaceport, from which you once again take a long elevator deep into the ocean. Outside the window dance the "Ribbons of Iret," enormous plumes of color rising up from from the abyss, only growing more intense the farther down you travel.`
				goto complex

			label waterlining
			`Traffic control gives you coordinates to the deepwater complex where the wedding is to take place, and you plunge the <ship> into the planet's ocean, its hull wrapped around by one of the "Ribbons of Iret," enormous and colorful. The farther down you travel, the more intense the bioluminescent plume grows, until it feels almost as if you are traveling through a nebula in space rather than an underwater bloom.`
			`	You reach the complex and dock at it, disembarking through an airlock and taking an elevator for the final short distance.`

			label complex
			`	You soon enter a similar room to the one you visited the last time you were here, though this one is even larger and more richly decorated, the walls a riot of color and form that is as ostentatious as it is impressive. A gentle mist issues from apertures on the vaulted ceiling and long golden threads trail downwards, writhing around particular Successors and eventually, you.`
			`	The thread inspects your face and clothing for a short time before it speaks in a soft, synthesized voice. "Greetings, Captain <first> <last>! Thou'rt authorized to attend the ceremony this afternoon and, following, a special meeting of the locally-gathered Houses." The voice continues for a while, providing you with information on which rooms to visit and how you are to find your way there.`
			`	Soon after, you catch sight of Khiajsore, the Myurej scion you spoke with before. They catch sight of you as well and slither towards you, batting away one of the threads with a bejeweled arm. "Captain, captain, delightful Captain," they say. "How pleasant of thee to accept our invitation."`
			choice
				`	"I appreciated your extending it."`
					goto appreciate
				`	"It's a very impressive facility you have here."`
			`	They hum. "Such beauty earns the envy of many; the natural and artificial intertwined."`
				goto khiajsore

			label appreciate
			`	"For such a unique and industrious figure, 'twould've been an unbearable snub not to!"`

			label khiajsore
			`	They rattle one of their arms a little, red gold and sparkling stones swinging through the air. "I just spoke of thee, in fact, with a delegate of House Seineq here, who confirmed what I've heard that thou wert of use to them as well! I think," they say, "thou didst set a good example for future aliens - benevolent, equitable, humble. Though I hear now Kaatrij has obtained thy vassalage? A boon to them, no doubt." Their face sparkles with color, eyes alight with furtive interest. "Though I hope for our efforts, Myurej has earned some measure of thy favor."`
			choice
				`	"I'm happy to help, so long as it doesn't conflict with my other responsibilities."`
				`	"I'm not sure I like where this is going."`
			`	Khiajsore laughs. "Of course, of course," they say. "Thou hast already helped us greatly. Now please excuse me."`
			`	They leave and two members of the crowd break off to follow them, which you notice carry small weapons strapped to their outfits. One of the golden threads makes its way back to you, informing you that the wedding ceremony will be beginning soon.`
			choice
				`	(Attend the wedding.)`
				`	(Wait around until the later meeting.)`
					goto skipped
			`	While most Successors are waiting outside the entrance to what must be a massive room, you are instead guided to an inconspicuous and out-of-the-way door, guarded by a pair of Successor soldiers. Neither one reacts to your attempt to pass, and as you step behind the door, it becomes clear why you aren't lining up with the general public: that massive room is entirely filled with water, a gigantic sphere with lights, platforms, and countless seats all built within it. A few small rooms like the one you now stand in are built into the walls like little transparent air bubbles at the shore of a great sea.`
			`	You are joined by three other Successors after a few minutes, each of whom takes their place in the little room. The ceremony begins shortly after. From apertures in the bottom of the sphere, legions of soldiers emerge, half wearing the colors of House Chydiyi and the other half of House Myurej. The two small armies swim around each other, interleaving their lines of bodies like the Ribbons themselves that you saw outside.`
			`	Only after a half hour of these acrobatics does the couple finally appear, rising up from the same apertures and joined by a flanking group of what must be the scions of their respective houses. You spy Khiajsore among them. There is a further intertwining, a display of finery and a ripple of many colors over the skin of those assembled, and then a collective hum rises from the crowd.`
			choice
				`	(Hum also.)`
				`	(Remain silent.)`
			`	With the moment apparently passed, speeches follow, each of the scions offering some short dialog about the history of their house and their hopes for its future. The translation device struggles to make sense of many of the words, as if they're being said in a dialect it's unfamiliar with. Eventually the ceremony seems to come to a close, the enormous audience trickling out of their seats and returning to mill about the facility.`

			label skipped
			`	You wait around for a little while until one of the threads comes to find you, giving you directions to an out-of-the-way room. Inside are representatives of all six High Houses; among them Khiajsore of House Myurej, Riijaaora of House Sioeora, and Kampa of House Kaatrij.`
			`	Kampa takes to the pool in the center of the room, addressing the group: "Honored representatives of the Houses assembled. House Kaatrij calls this union to make public our declaration of suzerainty to the alien captain <first> <last>. In keeping with the inter-Houses Treaty on Alien Agents, we herefore shall provide our vassal the violent fruits of our House, so that they might adequately and securely perform their duties.`
			`	In keeping with the Treaty, this offer may be extended by the other Houses in courtesy and deference to sovereign Kaatrij."`
			`	They step back to the rim of the pool and three others take to the pool's center: Myurej, Aqrabe, and Seineq. Each one speaks in turn, variations on a phrase: "In appreciation with the captain's service to our House, we provide our assent to and recognition of this offer."`
			`	Chydiyi's representative stays on the edge of the pool, abstaining from the discussion, but Sioeora's takes the center, glaring at you.`
			branch "kaatrij patron"
				has "successors kaatrij patron"

			`	"Despite Sioeora's generosity and patronage to the captain," Riijaaora says, "this alien sees fit to vassalize another House. We shall not recognize this relationship, nor open our outfitters to them."`
				goto license

			label "kaatrij patron"
			`	"Despite Sioeora's generosity to the captain," Riijaaora says, "this alien sees fit to vassalize another House. We shall not recognize this relationship, nor open our outfitters to them."`

			label license
			`	When they return to the edge, no more is said. Kampa returns to the pool and produces a small wooden box from their outfit, which they give to you.`
			choice
				`	(Take it.)`
			`	You open the box to find an elaborate gold brooch nestled among soft folds of velvet.`
			scene "outfit/high houses license"
			`	"Let this gift make clear to all thy responsibilities and privileges, and may thou have free access to all our House and allies offer..." Kampa says, "<first> <last>, Honored Knight-Vassal of the High House Kaatrij." A colorful display rushes over Kampa's skin and they pick up the brooch with one arm and pin it on your jacket right next to your translation device and the civilian license. The metal must be very dense; it is noticeably heavier than the others.`
			`	With this, the meeting concludes, the various members exiting in turn - the ones you've met before offering some short words of congratulations. You eventually exit as well, finding your way back through the facility. By a floral display you spy Saajret, apparently deep in conversation with Tiliia, the House Seineq engineer.`
			choice
				`	(Go speak with them.)`
				`	(Leave.)`
					goto end

			`	Tiliia spots you first, their skin breaking out in colors of excitement. "Saajret tells me of thine ascent to Kaatrij's ranks," they say. "Excellent that thou might be a concerted ally to mine own House as well."`
			`	Saajret hums and nods. "The captain is a canny sort," they say. "Capable of surviving our wiles, I believe." Tiliia laughs at that, Saajret continuing. "And Tiliia tells me thou wert of help to them as well, the reason by which our craft now gain an advantage through the wormhole."`
			label "saajret and tiliia"
			choice
				`	"It's good to see you two getting along."`
					to display
						not "Successors: getting along"
					goto "getting along"
				`	"Do you think Aqrabe and Kaatrij will be collaborating much?"`
					to display
						not "Successors: collaboration"
					goto collaboration
				`	"I'm still uncertain joining Kaatrij was the right choice."`
					to display
						not "Successors: uncertain"
					goto uncertain
				`	"I should get going."`
					goto end

			label "getting along"
			action
				"Successors: Ghosts Saajret Openness" ++
				set "Successors: getting along"
			`	Saajret nods. "Tiliia's work on the keystones that thou provided intrigues me greatly. It bears some resemblance to technologies I've studied in our archives - though the stellar metal shells are a wholly inventive solution, I believe."`
			`	Tiliia interjects at this, a hint of embarrassment on their skin. "T'was a matter of managing with what could be done," they say.`
			`	"Nonetheless," says Saajret, now to Tiliia, "A worthy achievement. I am glad for this little lull if only for the sake of collaboration."`
				goto "saajret and tiliia"

			label "collaboration"
			action
				set "Successors: collaboration"

			`	"'T'would be fruitful, doubtless," Tiliia says. "And now that Kaatrij opens up a little for the first time since their wound, perhaps 'tis not beyond the realm of possibility."`
			branch "low openness"
				"Successors: Ghosts Saajret Openness" < 0

			`	"I, too, would welcome it," Saajret adds. Their skin betrays a genuine satisfaction.`
				goto "saajret and tiliia"

			label "low openness"
			`	"I shall welcome it while it lasts," Saajret adds. "Though I fear Kaatrij's openness may be but a fleeting thing."`
				goto "saajret and tiliia"

			label "uncertain"
			action
				set "Successors: uncertain"
			branch "high forgiveness"
				"Successors: Ghosts Saajret Forgiveness" > 0

			`	Saajret hums deeply. "For us," they say, "our Houses are our families, and family is always a complicated thing. Perhaps I understand thee, captain, better than thou might imagine."`
				goto "saajret and tiliia"

			label "high forgiveness"
			`	Saajret hums, a shade of curiosity coming over them. "Perhaps 'tis more uncertain for thee," they say. "For us, our Houses are our families - we must endeavor to live with them, eccentricities and all."`
				goto "saajret and tiliia"

			label end
			action
				clear "Successors: getting along"
				clear "Successors: collaboration"
				clear "Successors: uncertain"
			`	You take the elevator back to your ship, catching one last brief glimpse of the Ribbons of Iret. As you leave, you receive a message from Kampa:`
			`	My congratulations once again. Thy service so far has been exemplary. Our House's efforts now focus on finding the identity of our attacker, a task, I fear, there is little thou can do t'accelerate. For now, thou might'st explore and prepare thyself for what may come in the future.`
			`	This I myself attest as J- S- Kampa, Fleet Captain to the High House Kaatrij.`



