			`The license you have received from House Kaatrij includes some cryptographic information that you might be able to use to decode the transmission you received from the drone ships. Would you like to do so?`
			choice
				`	(Yes.)`
				`	(No.)`
					decline

			branch "no resja"
				not "Successors: Ghosts Resja transmission"
			action
				log "People" "Resja" `(FILE "Lost"): [...] hastily, through the red chyme of the gullet of death [...] avian and [...] undefeated except in the battle over Avasaa-Novaa, which [...] and they have composed another in honor [...] named for the [...] of which there are nine, "four for the [...] and a final one missing, lost [...] lost [...]`
				log "People" "Resja" `(FILE "Heart"): [...] the destroyer whispers to the hero, "Not always was I what I am now [...] and took a spear and drove it deep into [...] heart [...] death [...] I find myself thinking much of this story [...] responsibility of knowing which thou art [...]`
				log "People" "Resja" `(FILE [...]): [...] I am starting to understand [...] which I why I must tell Saajret while [...]`

			label "no resja"

			branch "no queru"
				not "Successors: Ghosts Queru transmission"
			action
				log "People" "Resja" `(FILE "Trial"): [...] eight have gone on trial in the last [...] I was called upon to testify to the [...] do not know why they think I am an authority [...] absence [...] I sometimes wonder if [...] how it tastes [...]`

			label "no queru"

			branch "no hasur"
				not "Successors: Ghosts Hasur transmission"
			action
				log "People" "Resja" `(FILE "Emptiness"): [...] There was a terrible emptiness inside [...] grew larger with every blink [...] understood [...] envelop me. And long after I have died, long after the name of the Myiara fades to a future [...] that pang-ridden [...] will remain."`

			label "no hasur"

			`	In addition to the ship's flight telemetry and internal systems logs, the data recorder seems to contain a small number of text datablocks, badly degraded:`
			label files
			choice
				`	(FILE "Lost")`
					to display
						has "Successors: Ghosts Resja transmission"
					goto lost
				`	(FILE "Heart")`
					to display
						has "Successors: Ghosts Resja transmission"
					goto heart
				`	(FILE "Trial")`
					to display
						has "Successors: Ghosts Queru transmission"
					goto trial
				`	(FILE "Emptiness")`
					to display
						has "Successors: Ghosts Hasur transmission"
					goto emptiness
				`	(FILE [...])`
					to display
						has "Successors: Ghosts Resja transmission"
					goto lacuna
				`	(Exit.)`
					decline

			label lost
			`	[...] hastily, through the red chyme of the gullet of death [...] avian and [...] undefeated except in the battle over Avasaa-Novaa, which [...] and they have composed another in honor [...] named for the [...] of which there are nine, "four for the [...] and a final one missing, lost [...] lost [...]`
				goto files

			label heart
			`	[...] the destroyer whispers to the hero, "Not always was I what I am now [...] and took a spear and drove it deep into [...] heart [...] death [...] I find myself thinking much of this story [...] responsibility of knowing which thou art [...]`
				goto files

			label trial
			`	[...] eight have gone on trial in the last [...] I was called upon to testify to the [...] do not know why they think I am an authority [...] absence [...] I sometimes wonder if [...] how it tastes [...]`
				goto files

			label emptiness
			`	[...] There was a terrible emptiness inside [...] grew larger with every blink [...] understood [...] envelop me. And long after I have died, long after the name of the Myiara fades to a future [...] that pang-ridden [...] will remain."`
				goto files

			label lacuna
			action
				set "Successors: Ghosts Messages from the Past"
			`	[...] I am starting to understand how much I [...] so I must tell Saajret while [...]`
				goto files



mission "Successors: Ghosts Reincarnation"
	landing
	invisible
	source "Raaqa-Puan-Uuoru"
	to offer
		has "Successors: Ghosts Messages from the Past"
	on offer
		conversation
			`Would you like to speak to Saajret about finding their name in the file transmitted from Resja, of the Nine Eyes?`
			choice
				`	(Yes.)`
				`	(No.)`
					decline

			action
				"Successors: Ghosts Saajret Forgiveness" --
				"Successors: Ghosts Saajret Openness" ++
				set "Successors: Ghosts Saajret friend"
			`	Though it's a few minutes before your data-sphere missive is answered, Saajret soon invites you to join them in a nearby town, which proves to be only a half-hour away by spaceport shuttle. It is built into an amphitheatre-shaped cutout of a seaside cliff, terraced homes and shops emerging from the rock with their curious flowing Kaatrij architecture. Many share the sail-like projections of the main spaceport, some decorated with iridescent patterns that shimmer as the wind tosses them.`
			`	Saajret meets you at the regional spaceport, explaining that you caught them on a day off. They lead you through the town to one of the more elegant homes. It's shaped like a series of concentric semicircles, and they invite you into the outermost one, what you might call a receiving area with benches and indoor gardens. Small robots slither over the floors, attending to dust and water.`
			`	After a while, they turn to matters at hand. "Thou said that thou discover'd something about me in a transmission from the drone craft?" they ask. Though their tone is curious, something like a shade of fear lurks on their skin.`
			choice
				`	"It's probably just someone who shared your name, but I thought I'd tell you anyway. The transmissions included what seem like journals, and one of them mentions a 'Saajret.'"`
				`	"The transmissions included journals, and one of them mentions a 'Saajret.' Do you think they could have been an ancestor of yours?"`
			`	Something about hearing their name in this context seems to strike a discordant chord within Saajret. All at once confusion and anger and sorrow flit over them before they tense and their skin becomes a steely gray. They say nothing more on the matter, instead striking up a conversation about your recent experiences and never slowing. After an hour or so of catching up, they've finally had enough and let the conversation die.`
			`	As you leave, Saajret turns to you a final time. A strange expression is sitting on their face, and their skin seems incapable of resolving into a single color display. "Thou hast my deepest thanks, my friend," they say, sounding a little haunted, and close the door.`
				decline



