	description `The first prototype cloaks produced by the old House Kaatrij nearly eighteen hundred years ago were far from the adaptable and reliable technology they are today, each one consuming the power output of a large fusion reactor. Only once the House's engineers started to incorporate a ship's shielding into the cloak's operation was it made truly practical; hence, even today, the efficient cloak of the Vujlet-Usaqri relies on a steady stream of shield energy to operate. As a result, this modified variant of the Vujlet features a higher-capacity shield grid and more crew to maintain it.`
	description `	The Vujlet-Usaqri's cloaking technology is integrated with its hull and cannot be removed. Optimized for general use, it draws a moderate amount of fuel and shields while active.`
